rganizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/e4f43e0b49a51295b8055f645628f2bc9a5259df/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:16:34Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-12T11:16:34Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"TMA fields and exports, billing without the reception role, hideable menu\n\n- TMA: each core now answers user-defined fields (free text or one-click\n  options), editable at setup and mid-map; v1 maps migrate to a single field.\n  Export dialog: clipboard (TSV), CSV, PNG and print-to-PDF of a paper with\n  the map and the table.\n- Billing: drop the role gate and the reception view; \"Novo caso\" is a\n  primary button in the header that resets and returns to the specimen picker.\n- Sidebar lists only shipped tools and can be hidden entirely; the top bar\n  button brings it back.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"61d60afe498b6b1d5300bffd7e4a2e82e3475d1e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/61d60afe498b6b1d5300bffd7e4a2e82e3475d1e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/e4f43e0b49a51295b8055f645628f2bc9a5259df","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/e4f43e0b49a51295b8055f645628f2bc9a5259df","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKGU0ZjQzZTBiNDlhNTEyOTViODA1NWY2NDU2MjhmMmJjOWE1MjU5ZGY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/60117e6228f07243c9788f84aef0a09cfd8a9178","sha":"60117e6228f07243c9788f84aef0a09cfd8a9178","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/60117e6228f07243c9788f84aef0a09cfd8a9178"}],"sha":"e4f43e0b49a51295b8055f645628f2bc9a5259df","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/e4f43e0b49a51295b8055f645628f2bc9a5259df"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/60117e6228f07243c9788f84aef0a09cfd8a9178/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:05:22Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T17:05:22Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Drop the production and organizer tools; rebuild the macroscopy manual as code\n\n- Remove Controle de produção and Organizador de casos: pages, modules,\n  routes, landing snap, i18n sections and their Firestore rules.\n- Manual de macroscopia: one big card per system. The routines are\n  TypeScript modules under src/tools/macroscopy/content (no Firestore, no\n  in-app editor, no import/export); every placeholder protocol and the\n  seeded steps are gone, only the five systems remain.\n- TmaGrid: on first render only the map itself scrolls, never the window,\n  so the landing page stops opening at the TMA snap.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"93a37f7c1805eb155e78d009a28026614297dee4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/93a37f7c1805eb155e78d009a28026614297dee4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/60117e6228f07243c9788f84aef0a09cfd8a9178","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/60117e6228f07243c9788f84aef0a09cfd8a9178","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKDYwMTE3ZTYyMjhmMDcyNDNjOTc4OGY4NGFlZjBhMDljZmQ4YTkxNzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/236ffd9991652a1a2832e74a8dc5c80823761dce","sha":"236ffd9991652a1a2832e74a8dc5c80823761dce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/236ffd9991652a1a2832e74a8dc5c80823761dce"}],"sha":"60117e6228f07243c9788f84aef0a09cfd8a9178","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/60117e6228f07243c9788f84aef0a09cfd8a9178"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/236ffd9991652a1a2832e74a8dc5c80823761dce/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:33:15Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T16:33:15Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Bring the Just Cong frozen-section app in as the Congelação tool\n\nJust Cong was the default branch of Assistente-trabalho, cut down to the\nthree things a pathologist needs during an intraoperative consult: the\nfrozen-section report, the Mohs report and the saved templates. All three\ncome across.\n\nCongelação: header with hospital, patient, surgeon and pathologist; one\ncard per specimen with gross description, the receipt-sentence prefix,\nblocks derived from the cassette map, fragments, submission, cassette\nrows and the result; the four grossing masks (thyroid, breast, sentinel\nnode, fragments) that write the description — the sentinel-node one also\nfills the cassettes and the result. The cold-ischemia timer with the\ntyped-time override is the one commit the last merge left behind on the\nsentinel-lymph-node branch; it is in.\n\nMohs: main specimen with debulking, divisions on the clock face with the\nSVG diagram, axis rotation, ink colours and tumour-at-margin per sector,\nre-excisions with several fragments, one ischemia timer per stage, and\nthe cassette lines merged into ranges the way the original grouped them.\n\nOutput as before — copy, .txt, the paper report (print / PDF / PNG via\nhtml2canvas, loaded on demand) with the quadrant drawings, and the\nmailto with the \"Congelação HAC - date - initials\" subject. Templates\nkeep the Just Cong document shape under users/{uid}/frozen/modelos so\nanything saved there imports unchanged. The document in progress lives\nin localStorage per user, timers included, so a refresh mid-consult\nloses nothing.\n\nField labels inside the masks and the Mohs form stay in Portuguese, like\nthe stager''s calculator data: they are the bench vocabulary of a report\nthat is itself generated in Portuguese.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a3e3f4092e262ce9064ba238eda4f40945eaf6b1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/a3e3f4092e262ce9064ba238eda4f40945eaf6b1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/236ffd9991652a1a2832e74a8dc5c80823761dce","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/236ffd9991652a1a2832e74a8dc5c80823761dce","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKDIzNmZmZDk5OTE2NTJhMWEyODMyZTc0YThkYzVjODA4MjM3NjFkY2U","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/78688448f3cc644956640e01ab858068b975523f","sha":"78688448f3cc644956640e01ab858068b975523f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/78688448f3cc644956640e01ab858068b975523f"}],"sha":"236ffd9991652a1a2832e74a8dc5c80823761dce","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/236ffd9991652a1a2832e74a8dc5c80823761dce"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/78688448f3cc644956640e01ab858068b975523f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:15:46Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T14:15:46Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Bring Butcher Duck and Controle de Laudos in as two bench tools\n\nButcher Duck becomes the macroscopy manual: the same five systems and\n34 specimens, each routine written as a sequence of steps with a bench\nphoto, read one step at a time with the specimen in hand. The old CMS\n(Express + SQLite + admin password) is gone — the manual lives under the\nuser''s own Firestore document like the report archive, photos are\ndownscaled in the browser to fit the 1 MiB document, and the step text\nuses a three-rule dialect (## heading, - item, **bold**) rendered as\nReact nodes rather than injected HTML. The only routine that had content\n(uterine prolapse) comes seeded, deduplicated from six pasted copies;\nthe old JSON export still imports.\n\nControle de Laudos becomes the sign-out tracker, feature for feature:\nsession clock, cases logged with slide counts, third-party and frozen\nflags, pauses, several sessions per day, the speedometers against best\nday / overall / month, the work-vs-pause pie, the collapsible history\nwith delete at every level, records by day/week/month and the period\nstatistics with segment chips and stacked bars. The day is keyed to\nlocal time, not UTC, so an evening session no longer becomes tomorrow.\nIts own Firebase project (laudos-a7009) is left behind; data sits under\nthe user in this one, so both tools share the account and the rules.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"aff3714c47af696e8993af66a107dd0202c6832f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/aff3714c47af696e8993af66a107dd0202c6832f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/78688448f3cc644956640e01ab858068b975523f","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/78688448f3cc644956640e01ab858068b975523f","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKDc4Njg4NDQ4ZjNjYzY0NDk1NjY0MGUwMWFiODU4MDY4Yjk3NTUyM2Y","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/4e566b4ba8462f7127f39523af5801fec554d65c","sha":"4e566b4ba8462f7127f39523af5801fec554d65c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/4e566b4ba8462f7127f39523af5801fec554d65c"}],"sha":"78688448f3cc644956640e01ab858068b975523f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/78688448f3cc644956640e01ab858068b975523f"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/4e566b4ba8462f7127f39523af5801fec554d65c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T11:40:14Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T11:40:14Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Rebuild the home page as one screen per working tool\n\nThe landing sold the toolkit with prose and cards: a subtitle, four\nsample chips, four value propositions and a grid of every tool in the\nqueue. None of it showed a tool doing anything.\n\nNow the page snaps screen by screen, and each screen is the tool itself\nrunning on a case already half entered — the visitor types in the table\nand watches the numbers, the 3D specimen and the report text move.\nProstate and breast lead with the cassette table beside the model and\nthe assembled report below; then staging, field conversion, CBHPM\nbilling, the report archive, the case organizer and the TMA mapper.\n\nNothing here writes to storage: the demos hold their own state, so a\nsigned-in visitor''s real case is never touched, and the closing screen\nis where the account comes in.\n\nThe snap is mandatory only where a whole screen fits (>= 1440 x 900);\nanywhere narrower or shorter it falls back to proximity, which never\ntraps the scroll, and reduced-motion turns it off. three.js is loaded\nper demo when its screen comes near, so the first paint stays light.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015QKVAHL4wsBAXRKjwQv5r1","tree":{"sha":"f7e97d01d3f71ca8082f3df9a3d2296cab1125f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/f7e97d01d3f71ca8082f3df9a3d2296cab1125f4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/4e566b4ba8462f7127f39523af5801fec554d65c","verification":{"payload":"tree f7e97d01d3f71ca8082f3df9a3d2296cab1125f4\nparent 3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788954014 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1788954014 +0000\n\nRebuild the home page as one screen per working tool\n\nThe landing sold the toolkit with prose and cards: a subtitle, four\nsample chips, four value propositions and a grid of every tool in the\nqueue. None of it showed a tool doing anything.\n\nNow the page snaps screen by screen, and each screen is the tool itself\nrunning on a case already half entered — the visitor types in the table\nand watches the numbers, the 3D specimen and the report text move.\nProstate and breast lead with the cassette table beside the model and\nthe assembled report below; then staging, field conversion, CBHPM\nbilling, the report archive, the case organizer and the TMA mapper.\n\nNothing here writes to storage: the demos hold their own state, so a\nsigned-in visitor''s real case is never touched, and the closing screen\nis where the account comes in.\n\nThe snap is mandatory only where a whole screen fits (>= 1440 x 900);\nanywhere narrower or shorter it falls back to proximity, which never\ntraps the scroll, and reduced-motion turns it off. three.js is loaded\nper demo when its screen comes near, so the first paint stays light.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_015QKVAHL4wsBAXRKjwQv5r1\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQHx7zUKv\n1DCr+jTQ6ePizA/6Qn8Ey5HehoFatvjQc1mqXHqGpoHXwLqeQInG9vCBD7X5EDhK9Z3QPv1I1Dwd\nHQ4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-09T11:40:22Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/4e566b4ba8462f7127f39523af5801fec554d65c","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKDRlNTY2YjRiYTg0NjJmNzEyN2YzOTUyM2FmNTgwMWZlYzU1NGQ2NWM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479","sha":"3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479"}],"sha":"4e566b4ba8462f7127f39523af5801fec554d65c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/4e566b4ba8462f7127f39523af5801fec554d65c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T21:51:20Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T21:51:20Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Add the breast mapper: grossing in 3D and RCB sign-out\n\nTwo modules over one map. At grossing: specimen, inked margins, lesions\nplaced by dragging or by margin distances, slicing, cassette grid of the\nlargest cross-section, the gross description, an A4 image and a map code.\nAt sign-out: rebuild the map (code, local import or by hand), score %CA\nand %CIS per cassette next to the MD Anderson cellularity guide, lymph\nnodes, and the Residual Cancer Burden with ypT/ypN suggested.\n\nShared form fields and the canvas report helpers move out of the prostate\ntool so both mappers use them.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"3f28009901ef9a6a6b9ce21cdd54133df052ce25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/3f28009901ef9a6a6b9ce21cdd54133df052ce25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKDNjYmJhMmY3M2JmYmQxYzU4ZGZlMDY5OTZiOTc5MDI2Yjg2Mjc0Nzk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/b82eb794793fdf7e701f26e2fb26ebb959f72664","sha":"b82eb794793fdf7e701f26e2fb26ebb959f72664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/b82eb794793fdf7e701f26e2fb26ebb959f72664"}],"sha":"3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/3cbba2f73bfbd1c58dfe06996b979026b8627479"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/b82eb794793fdf7e701f26e2fb26ebb959f72664/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T21:51:20Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T21:51:20Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Add the mm² → fields conversion to the field converter\n\nDigital slides count per area, but report templates still ask for \"per\n10 fields\": the converter now runs in both directions, with the\nmicroscope''s field at the chosen objective and the reference-field chips.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"03d5b06c275fcfb1d42b284d9cb639d9e102c416","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/03d5b06c275fcfb1d42b284d9cb639d9e102c416"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/b82eb794793fdf7e701f26e2fb26ebb959f72664","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/b82eb794793fdf7e701f26e2fb26ebb959f72664","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKGI4MmViNzk0NzkzZmRmN2U3MDFmMjZlMmZiMjZlYmI5NTlmNzI2NjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/a169bc3865a360d7f5fe7514396a14c4dcc880a5","sha":"a169bc3865a360d7f5fe7514396a14c4dcc880a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a169bc3865a360d7f5fe7514396a14c4dcc880a5"}],"sha":"b82eb794793fdf7e701f26e2fb26ebb959f72664","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/b82eb794793fdf7e701f26e2fb26ebb959f72664"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a169bc3865a360d7f5fe7514396a14c4dcc880a5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T15:24:19Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T15:24:19Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Rebuild the CBHPM tool around the specimen on the bench\n\nThe wizard asked abstract questions (\"how many margins?\") and only ever\ncovered one chapter per run. What actually goes wrong at the lab is a\nbig specimen billed short by the front desk, so the tool now starts from\nwho is using it and, for the pathologist, from the specimen itself.\n\nPicking \"radical prostatectomy\" lists its structures by name — bladder\nneck, apical and circumferential margins, both seminal vesicles and vasa\ndeferentia, the node groups — already ticked where they are the norm; he\nunticks what he did not examine and can add a structure of his own or\nsave the adjusted list as his template. Every tick is one 22-6, capped at\n3 or 5 by specimen type. Case, complements (immunos, stains, frozen\nsection, review, molecular, EM) and the front desk''s entry all add up in\none bill, with a side-by-side check of what is already booked and what is\nmissing.\n\nReception keeps its own, shorter path: name of the material, number of\nflasks, entry code, plus a note on what only the report can settle.\n\nCatalogue: 67 specimens across ten systems, accent-insensitive search.\nVerified against the handbook''s worked examples (Whipple, mastectomy,\nradical hysterectomies, cone, sentinel node, frozen section, FNA, IHC\npanels) in a throwaway node harness.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4e7f777996dc5e7b69c70c9d3a90ead5a7537799","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/4e7f777996dc5e7b69c70c9d3a90ead5a7537799"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/a169bc3865a360d7f5fe7514396a14c4dcc880a5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/a169bc3865a360d7f5fe7514396a14c4dcc880a5","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKGExNjliYzM4NjVhMzYwZDdmNWZlNzUxNDM5NmExNGM0ZGNjODgwYTU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/a427bd82ffe61716c5cf453d187a205eac7a4591","sha":"a427bd82ffe61716c5cf453d187a205eac7a4591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a427bd82ffe61716c5cf453d187a205eac7a4591"}],"sha":"a169bc3865a360d7f5fe7514396a14c4dcc880a5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a169bc3865a360d7f5fe7514396a14c4dcc880a5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a427bd82ffe61716c5cf453d187a205eac7a4591/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:38:23Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:38:23Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Export the prostate case as an A4 image; colour by worst pattern\n\nA button on the result step renders a PNG in A4 proportions with the\nPatholytics header, the summary tiles (volume, Gleason, grade group,\npattern 4 with the cribriform status, pattern 5), the cassette strip\nmap, the per-cassette table (two columns when long) and anterior and\nposterior views of the 3D model rendered off-screen at fixed cameras.\nThe map keeps its size; the table and the views take what is left.\n\nCassette colours now follow the worst pattern present - 3 green,\n4 yellow, 5 red - in the 2D map, the table and the 3D model, with tumour\n% as intensity. The 3D frame is now anatomically right-handed (+x is the\npatient right), so the anterior view shows the right side on the left\nand the posterior view on the right, as at the bench.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"48e667f3001c03de4ef0a7e8a6b36bb028fea725","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/48e667f3001c03de4ef0a7e8a6b36bb028fea725"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/a427bd82ffe61716c5cf453d187a205eac7a4591","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/a427bd82ffe61716c5cf453d187a205eac7a4591","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKGE0MjdiZDgyZmZlNjE3MTZjNWNmNDUzZDE4N2EyMDVlYWM3YTQ1OTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/c15f713579f70da99027c7bd59d621daae28c85b","sha":"c15f713579f70da99027c7bd59d621daae28c85b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/c15f713579f70da99027c7bd59d621daae28c85b"}],"sha":"a427bd82ffe61716c5cf453d187a205eac7a4591","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a427bd82ffe61716c5cf453d187a205eac7a4591"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/c15f713579f70da99027c7bd59d621daae28c85b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:04:55Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-04T14:04:55Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Cut the 3D prostate along the cassette planes\n\nApex and base cones are now small caps (about 9% of the length each)\ninstead of a third of the gland. The mesh is generated on a\nlatitude/longitude grid whose rings coincide with every cut between\ncassettes and whose meridians sit exactly on the midline and the\nlateral plane, so no face straddles a boundary and colours end on the\nline; the divider lines are analytic curves on the surface rather than\ntriangle edges (which zig-zagged), and analytic ellipsoid normals give\nsmooth shading instead of per-face banding.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e9ef0485684b0bcaad626ed61cb064661f0273db","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/e9ef0485684b0bcaad626ed61cb064661f0273db"},"url":"https://