}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/a3a9086e2c6a78887e6531228fe3d30ac4926349","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKGEzYTkwODZlMmM2YTc4ODg3ZTY1MzEyMjhmZTNkMzBhYzQ5MjYzNDk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134","sha":"a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134"},{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/e9be76eaf5aee9c0fad102ba7fe48e40186cdf27","sha":"e9be76eaf5aee9c0fad102ba7fe48e40186cdf27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/e9be76eaf5aee9c0fad102ba7fe48e40186cdf27"}],"sha":"a3a9086e2c6a78887e6531228fe3d30ac4926349","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a3a9086e2c6a78887e6531228fe3d30ac4926349"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/e9be76eaf5aee9c0fad102ba7fe48e40186cdf27/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T17:45:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T17:45:33Z","email":"noreply@anthropic.com","name":"Claude"},"message":"Add the case organiser with user-defined lists and stages\n\nPorts the personal case organiser into Patholytics as a tool anyone can\nshape to their own workflow. The original hardcoded six statuses, a\ntwelve-digit FAP and an \"is there immuno pending?\" question on release;\nnone of that survives as a fixed concept.\n\nWhat each user defines instead: any number of lists (up to ten stages\neach), the stage names, colours and emoji, and the label the identifier\nfield carries. Four templates seed a new list — the surgical pathology\nflow among them — and every stage stays editable afterwards, including\napplying a different template later, which asks where the existing cases\nland rather than stranding them.\n\nTwo structural changes over the original. Blocked is a marker rather than\na stage, so a case no longer has to choose between \"reported\" and\n\"pending\" and lose where it was. Archiving is independent of the stage,\nso reopening restores the case exactly where it stood.\n\nKept as they were, because they earned it: the expandable row, the\nappend-only update log with timestamps, the deadline countdown in three\nbands, manual reordering, the optional tick with a stamp, bulk delete and\none-click copy of the identifier. Added: search, ready-made sort orders,\nmoving a case between lists, and a real mobile layout.\n\nUnlike the other tools, this one stores in Firestore rather than the\nbrowser: the data accumulates over weeks and is read from both phone and\ndesktop. Rules restrict every list and case to its owner. The free-plan\nceiling is written but switched off until billing exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AtXGgi37wQDj94gGEJkd9f","tree":{"sha":"9996db86192410803b2648d918e8f5b48909c202","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/9996db86192410803b2648d918e8f5b48909c202"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/e9be76eaf5aee9c0fad102ba7fe48e40186cdf27","verification":{"payload":"tree 9996db86192410803b2648d918e8f5b48909c202\nparent a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134\nauthor Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787679933 +0000\ncommitter Claude <noreply@anthropic.com> 1787679933 +0000\n\nAdd the case organiser with user-defined lists and stages\n\nPorts the personal case organiser into Patholytics as a tool anyone can\nshape to their own workflow. The original hardcoded six statuses, a\ntwelve-digit FAP and an \"is there immuno pending?\" question on release;\nnone of that survives as a fixed concept.\n\nWhat each user defines instead: any number of lists (up to ten stages\neach), the stage names, colours and emoji, and the label the identifier\nfield carries. Four templates seed a new list — the surgical pathology\nflow among them — and every stage stays editable afterwards, including\napplying a different template later, which asks where the existing cases\nland rather than stranding them.\n\nTwo structural changes over the original. Blocked is a marker rather than\na stage, so a case no longer has to choose between \"reported\" and\n\"pending\" and lose where it was. Archiving is independent of the stage,\nso reopening restores the case exactly where it stood.\n\nKept as they were, because they earned it: the expandable row, the\nappend-only update log with timestamps, the deadline countdown in three\nbands, manual reordering, the optional tick with a stamp, bulk delete and\none-click copy of the identifier. Added: search, ready-made sort orders,\nmoving a case between lists, and a real mobile layout.\n\nUnlike the other tools, this one stores in Firestore rather than the\nbrowser: the data accumulates over weeks and is read from both phone and\ndesktop. Rules restrict every list and case to its owner. The free-plan\nceiling is written but switched off until billing exists.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AtXGgi37wQDj94gGEJkd9f\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgrLzsfFISF4by8Q+FKz27YpkK1USsBB+m\namu1QkJnbDsAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAQNwqQKI9\n3KGt2f9Wx5C8VNsZGkO24CKZ2PUnmHOh3STKHZzxkgTzHgCg+7yDviV9Cr1wjcS19JUVS3zE1rG0\ndg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-08-25T17:45:43Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/81847?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/claude","id":81847,"login":"claude","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjgxODQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/claude","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/e9be76eaf5aee9c0fad102ba7fe48e40186cdf27","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKGU5YmU3NmVhZjVhZWU5YzBmYWQxMDJiYTdmZTQ4ZTQwMTg2Y2RmMjc","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134","sha":"a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134"}],"sha":"e9be76eaf5aee9c0fad102ba7fe48e40186cdf27","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/e9be76eaf5aee9c0fad102ba7fe48e40186cdf27"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-25T00:01:59Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-25T00:01:59Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Fix the 3D prostate canvas overflowing on scaled displays\n\nrenderer.setSize was called with updateStyle=false, so the canvas kept\nits attribute size (CSS pixels x devicePixelRatio) and overflowed the\ncontainer on Windows displays scaled above 100%, showing only a corner\nof the specimen. Let three.js set the canvas CSS size too.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0e658f576f310db29884228dd77265e81627489d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/0e658f576f310db29884228dd77265e81627489d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKGE0NWQ2YjliM2UwMjE0MTJhYjliNWZlMzI1MDRiN2JmMzJlY2ExMzQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/86d07e5aa4ba18224d8a43cdb47faf8d7fd6b51a","sha":"86d07e5aa4ba18224d8a43cdb47faf8d7fd6b51a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/86d07e5aa4ba18224d8a43cdb47faf8d7fd6b51a"}],"sha":"a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/a45d6b9b3e021412ab9b5fe32504b7bf32eca134"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/86d07e5aa4ba18224d8a43cdb47faf8d7fd6b51a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T23:54:28Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T23:54:28Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Add the prostatectomy mapper with weighted Gleason and 2D/3D maps\n\nNew tool at /tools/prostate (replaces the coming-soon Gleason entry):\ndescribe the grossing grid (transverse slices x angular sectors, plus\napex/base cones cut right-to-left, with per-cassette label overrides and\nsaved templates), enter tumour %, G4/G5, margins (mm + Gleason at the\nmargin) and focal/established EPE per cassette, and get the volume, the\ntumour-weighted Gleason score under the ISUP 2014/2019 prostatectomy\nrules (minor lower-grade pattern <=5% ignored, higher-grade third\npattern as tertiary when <=5%, secondary when above), cribriform and\nintraductal carcinoma globally or per cassette, per-region breakdowns,\nlaterality, and a suggested pT/pN/R — summarised as copyable parameters\nfor the report, not as a report.\n\nThe specimen is drawn twice from the same cells: an SVG slice map\n(discs seen from the base, radiological convention) and a procedural\n3D model (three.js, lazy-loaded on this page only) with the dominant\nGleason pattern as the heat hue and tumour % as intensity, plus margin\nand EPE markers. Case state and grid templates persist per user in\nlocalStorage.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"872d294ca5d026df90e96d695ae4b0d075570309","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/872d294ca5d026df90e96d695ae4b0d075570309"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/86d07e5aa4ba18224d8a43cdb47faf8d7fd6b51a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/86d07e5aa4ba18224d8a43cdb47faf8d7fd6b51a","node_id":"C_kwDOT-2Hc9oAKDg2ZDA3ZTVhYTRiYTE4MjI0ZDhhNDNjZGI0N2ZhZjhkN2ZkNmI1MWE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111/Patholytics/commit/b609f2c55b93afdc89acd2f70ca3cd9b23cb6062","sha":"b609f2c55b93afdc89acd2f70ca3cd9b23cb6062","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/b609f2c55b93afdc89acd2f70ca3cd9b23cb6062"}],"sha":"86d07e5aa4ba18224d8a43cdb47faf8d7fd6b51a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/86d07e5aa4ba18224d8a43cdb47faf8d7fd6b51a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_kgDOD4ChiQ","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/commits/b609f2c55b93afdc89acd2f70ca3cd9b23cb6062/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T23:54:28Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T23:54:28Z","email":"motag19@yahoo.com","name":"guimota111"},"message":"Add a light theme and a light/dark/system switcher\n\nPromote the token palette to a light default and move the original\ndark palette under `html.dark`, so components keep referencing the same\ntokens. The preference (light, dark, or follow the OS) is stored in the\nbrowser; an inline script in index.html resolves it before first paint\nto avoid a theme flash, and src/lib/theme.ts keeps <html> and the\ntheme-color meta in sync afterwards. The switcher sits next to the\nlanguage switcher in both the marketing and signed-in headers.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"397a1a34214e9481ed4fc0ba76a606fba3017d9b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/trees/397a1a34214e9481ed4fc0ba76a606fba3017d9b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/guimota111/Patholytics/git/commits/b609f2c55b93afdc89acd2f70ca3cd9b23cb6062","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/260088201?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/guimota111/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/guimota111","id":260088201,"login":"guimota111","node_id":"U_k