:{"date":"2026-09-22T08:43:50Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"🔑 feat(action): passes an optional PR_LENS_TOKEN through to the CLI","tree":{"sha":"b55323861ef3fcc2998c6aeacd1cb12c9f647638","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/b55323861ef3fcc2998c6aeacd1cb12c9f647638"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/98d8a943ccf9cb52f9c242dd15b4198f36e82616","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/98d8a943ccf9cb52f9c242dd15b4198f36e82616","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKDk4ZDhhOTQzY2NmOWNiNTJmOWMyNDJkZDE1YjQxOThmMzZlODI2MTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/b42d18e3fa52402a2119b6b326d30a91205ddb38","sha":"b42d18e3fa52402a2119b6b326d30a91205ddb38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/b42d18e3fa52402a2119b6b326d30a91205ddb38"}],"sha":"98d8a943ccf9cb52f9c242dd15b4198f36e82616","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/98d8a943ccf9cb52f9c242dd15b4198f36e82616"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/b42d18e3fa52402a2119b6b326d30a91205ddb38/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:45:57Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T06:45:57Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"✨ feat(cli): names the machine that mints a canvas\n\nA canvas has no owner today, and the write token is the only thing that\ncan reach it. Lose the checkout and it is unreachable by anyone, because\nthe app keeps a hash and cannot hand the token back.\n\nSo every mint now carries an install id: a machine-level secret kept at\n$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/pr-lens/installs/, which a later sign-in can link to an\naccount to claim everything that machine has pushed.\n\nOne id per store, not one per machine. The id is what will link a machine\nto an account, so whoever holds it can have that machine''s canvases\nattributed to them; sending the same one to every --api would hand that to\na private store, or to a host someone was talked into passing.\n\nAttribution never costs a push. No home directory, an unreadable file, a\nread-only disk, no entropy — every failure answers undefined and the mint\ngoes out unattributed, exactly as it did before this existed.\n\nEach file is made by exclusive create and then left alone, so two first\nruns settle without a lock. A file whose bytes were read and say nothing\nusable is repaired; one that merely could not be read is never touched,\nbecause unlinking is governed by the directory rather than the file, and a\nrun that cannot read an id can still destroy it.\n\nRedirects are refused rather than followed. The runtime strips\nauthorization across origins but forwards everything else, so a hop would\ncarry the install id to whichever host answered. Every route replies\ndirectly, so a 3xx now names the address it points at instead of being\nobeyed.\n\nDocumented under Mint and Conventions in docs/canvas-api.md: both are\ncontract changes a private store needs, and they ship here rather than\nwith the rest of the protocol work.","tree":{"sha":"d7f505c77bdb762ff05c2a4e0316e559850b38a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/d7f505c77bdb762ff05c2a4e0316e559850b38a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/b42d18e3fa52402a2119b6b326d30a91205ddb38","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/b42d18e3fa52402a2119b6b326d30a91205ddb38","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKGI0MmQxOGUzZmE1MjQwMmEyMTE5YjZiMzI2ZDMwYTkxMjA1ZGRiMzg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/ce81274c292706e39dac58d25e9e21c295a3dd86","sha":"ce81274c292706e39dac58d25e9e21c295a3dd86","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/ce81274c292706e39dac58d25e9e21c295a3dd86"}],"sha":"b42d18e3fa52402a2119b6b326d30a91205ddb38","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/b42d18e3fa52402a2119b6b326d30a91205ddb38"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/ddde68bfd7bdd887eb13510e0b567addfb2ef7c2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:59:36Z","email":"favour@coldtea.ai","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:59:36Z","email":"favour@coldtea.ai","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"📝 doc(bitbucket): shows the step form, so the pipe is not the only way in\n\nA pipe is a Docker image, so adopting one means an image has been published — and none has. The same script runs as an ordinary step on node:20, which needs nothing published at all.\n\nThis is not a second implementation: it is the same pipe/lens.sh, which already defaults every variable it reads, so a step needs the same two secrets the pipe does and nothing else. It is also the shape the GitHub Action uses.\n\nWhat a step gives up is discovery — a pipe appears in Atlassian''s listing and is one line to adopt. That trade is the consumer''s to make, and until the image ships it is the only one available.","tree":{"sha":"8e70d7c5afc19437417630b4554d45c3ff9424d1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/8e70d7c5afc19437417630b4554d45c3ff9424d1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/ddde68bfd7bdd887eb13510e0b567addfb2ef7c2","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/ddde68bfd7bdd887eb13510e0b567addfb2ef7c2","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKGRkZGU2OGJmZDdiZGQ4ODdlYjEzNTEwZTBiNTY3YWRkZmIyZWY3YzI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/7cd7a7aba8b31bb64c0aeed381798963f9c5d811","sha":"7cd7a7aba8b31bb64c0aeed381798963f9c5d811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/7cd7a7aba8b31bb64c0aeed381798963f9c5d811"}],"sha":"ddde68bfd7bdd887eb13510e0b567addfb2ef7c2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/ddde68bfd7bdd887eb13510e0b567addfb2ef7c2"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/7cd7a7aba8b31bb64c0aeed381798963f9c5d811/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:59:36Z","email":"favour@coldtea.ai","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T15:59:36Z","email":"favour@coldtea.ai","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"🗑️  chore(gitlab): drops the image, and the version pinned twice with it\n\nThe component now fetches the CLI from npm on each run, which is exactly what the GitHub Action has always done.\n\nThe image existed to avoid executing whatever the registry served that minute inside a job holding the customer''s CI variables. That risk is real — and it is one the GitHub path, the mature one, already lives with on every run. What the image bought in return was a CLI version pinned by hand in two places that had to move in lockstep, which is the half of COL-1486 that merging does not fix, plus an unpublished image nobody could use and a test for it that could not run.\n\nConsistency is the argument: keep it on all three forges or none. Bitbucket has no choice — a pipe is a Docker image — but GitLab did, and this was the one place with the least justification for it.\n\nIf the per-run fetch is worth removing, the way to remove it is an integrity hash on all three, not one image on one forge.","tree":{"sha":"c4895cd71b831c70b795ca18b93e04790b0b1c2f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/c4895cd71b831c70b795ca18b93e04790b0b1c2f"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/7cd7a7aba8b31bb64c0aeed381798963f9c5d811","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/7cd7a7aba8b31bb64c0aeed381798963f9c5d811","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKDdjZDdhN2FiYThiMzFiYjY0YzBhZWVkMzgxNzk4OTYzZjljNWQ4MTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/8f28cf84ad2085e3fb7a20d005a97ad20972ab8a","sha":"8f28cf84ad2085e3fb7a20d005a97ad20972ab8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/8f28cf84ad2085e3fb7a20d005a97ad20972ab8a"}],"sha":"7cd7a7aba8b31bb64c0aeed381798963f9c5d811","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/7cd7a7aba8b31bb64c0aeed381798963f9c5d811"},{"author":null,"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/8f28cf84ad2085e3fb7a20d005a97ad20972ab8a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T10:49:34Z","email":"favour@coldtea.ai","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T10:49:34Z","email":"favour@coldtea.ai","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"🔗 fix(gitlab): makes the action link work outside the monorepo","tree":{"sha":"5c1defee021ec870edbdba24992fd66ffe82f238","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/5c1defee021ec870edbdba24992fd66ffe82f238"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/8f28cf84ad2085e3fb7a20d005a97ad20972ab8a","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":null,"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/8f28cf84ad2085e3fb7a20d005a97ad20972ab8a","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKDhmMjhjZjg0YWQyMDg1ZTNmYjdhMjBkMDA1YTk3YWQyMDk3MmFiOGE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/2fb23382937b5da9802d4eeeac8dcaf4d5c6aeef","sha":"2fb23382937b5da9802d4eeeac8dcaf4d5c6aeef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/2fb23382937b5da9802d4eeeac8dcaf4d5c6aeef"}],"sha":"8f28cf84ad2085e3fb7a20d005a97ad20972ab8a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/8f28cf84ad2085e3fb7a20d005a97ad20972ab8a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/2fb23382937b5da9802d4eeeac8dcaf4d5c6aeef/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:04:08Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:04:08Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"🔍 chore(bitbucket): prints why a refused Code Insights report was refused\n\n`report_type` is omitted on purpose — Bitbucket''s four values all assert\nsomething about the code, and a diagram asserts none of them — but that\njudgement was made without a live API to check it against. Swallowing the\nrefusal meant the only way to learn it was wrong would be a customer\nnoticing the Reports tab stays empty.\n\nStill fail-soft; the comment is the product.","tree":{"sha":"584da987114f7a848007f432ba5de1429bc8de65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/584da987114f7a848007f432ba5de1429bc8de65"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/2fb23382937b5da9802d4eeeac8dcaf4d5c6aeef","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/2fb23382937b5da9802d4eeeac8dcaf4d5c6aeef","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKDJmYjIzMzgyOTM3YjVkYTk4MDJkNGVlZWFjOGRjYWY0ZDVjNmFlZWY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/0140dc86321544a72880f2a3611d5500ede5ec89","sha":"0140dc86321544a72880f2a3611d5500ede5ec89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/0140dc86321544a72880f2a3611d5500ede5ec89"}],"sha":"2fb23382937b5da9802d4eeeac8dcaf4d5c6aeef","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/2fb23382937b5da9802d4eeeac8dcaf4d5c6aeef"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/0140dc86321544a72880f2a3611d5500ede5ec89/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:02:23Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T08:02:23Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"🎯 fix(schema,renderer): stops a caller asking for more themes than the cap assumes\n\n`MAX_VIEWS` is derived from the pair, on the argument that `neutral`\nreplaces the pair rather than joining it. The argument is right and the\nnumber is right, but nothing enforced it: `renderAll` took\n`readonly Theme[]`, so a caller passing all three emitted three assets per\nview against a budget that assumed two — a document that validates producing\na manifest that does not, which is exactly the promise this package exists\nto make.\n\n`RenderThemes` admits the pair, one half of it, or the single neutral. The\ncompiler found the one caller that had drifted the moment the type landed.\n\nThe comment above `MAX_RENDER_ASSETS` still said the cap was \"the worst\ncase, every theme rendered\", which was true when the divisor was the enum\nand false since the third theme arrived. It says what it means now, and\nnames the type that keeps it honest.","tree":{"sha":"5fea7e063d120436a9b826b6aabe2ea045f260a8","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/5fea7e063d120436a9b826b6aabe2ea045f260a8"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/0140dc86321544a72880f2a3611d5500ede5ec89","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/0140dc86321544a72880f2a3611d5500ede5ec89","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKDAxNDBkYzg2MzIxNTQ0YTcyODgwZjJhMzYxMWQ1NTAwZWRlNWVjODk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/d90a295888d2056fbad15a44272b5063de8435c1","sha":"d90a295888d2056fbad15a44272b5063de8435c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/d90a295888d2056fbad15a44272b5063de8435c1"}],"sha":"0140dc86321544a72880f2a3611d5500ede5ec89","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/0140dc86321544a72880f2a3611d5500ede5ec89"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/d90a295888d2056fbad15a44272b5063de8435c1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:44:45Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:44:45Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"📊 feat(bitbucket): records the run on the pull request''s Reports tab\n\nThe comment is one artefact competing with every other bot in a busy pull\nrequest, and it collapses. A Code Insights report puts PR Lens where a\nreviewer looks for what ran on a commit, with a link to the drawing and the\ntwo numbers worth knowing.\n\nDeliberately untyped. Bitbucket''s report types are SECURITY, COVERAGE, TEST\nand BUG, and a diagram is none of them — claiming one files a drawing in\nsomebody''s defect tooling under a heading it does not belong to. For the\nsame reason there are no annotations: those render as findings against\nlines, and PR Lens does not produce findings.\n\nGitLab''s Code Quality artifact is declined for that reason and not\nimplemented. Its entries carry a severity and a file location and render as\nissues in the merge request widget; the only way to appear there is to\ninvent a finding. The component already publishes the render as a job\nartifact and sets a commit status, which is the honest version of the same\nidea.\n\nFail-soft, because this is the second surface: a Bitbucket that will not\ntake the report must not fail a run whose comment was posted. Verified by\nmutation — removing the guard fails the test, and so does labelling the\nreport as a defect type.\n\nFound while testing: the new blocks use `node -e`, where the first argument\nis argv[1] — the rest of this script uses `node -`, where it is argv[2].\nReading the arguments the wrong way made the report link the string \"0\".","tree":{"sha":"be802518784cf6dd50e4bcb8f0413cf1e7d210d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/be802518784cf6dd50e4bcb8f0413cf1e7d210d0"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/d90a295888d2056fbad15a44272b5063de8435c1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/d90a295888d2056fbad15a44272b5063de8435c1","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKGQ5MGEyOTU4ODhkMjA1NmZiYWQxNWE0NDI3MmI1MDYzZGU4NDM1YzE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/20236ead1faeee35c28c70ec9ab52a91716aab65","sha":"20236ead1faeee35c28c70ec9ab52a91716aab65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/20236ead1faeee35c28c70ec9ab52a91716aab65"}],"sha":"d90a295888d2056fbad15a44272b5063de8435c1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/d90a295888d2056fbad15a44272b5063de8435c1"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/20236ead1faeee35c28c70ec9ab52a91716aab65/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:38:39Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:38:39Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"📦 chore(gitlab,bitbucket): gives both packages a way to be released\n\nNeither could be installed by a stranger. The component is in the CI/CD\ncatalog only if a tagged commit was released with the `release` keyword —\nwithout one it works for anyone who already knows its path and is findable\nby nobody, which defeats shipping a component rather than a snippet to copy.\nThe release job lives beside the component it releases rather than only in\nthe gitlab.com mirror, along with the mirror''s other requirements: README\nand templates/ at its own root, a project description, and the catalog\ntoggle enabled.\n\nThe mirror also verifies that the template still embeds scripts/lens.sh\nverbatim. That is the one thing a mirror can get wrong on its own, and\ngetting it wrong publishes a component whose script is not the one this\nrepository tests.\n\nBoth packages have a changelog now, with the versioning policy stated in it:\nwhat a consumer who pinned a major can expect a minor to do to them. Pinning\na version with no way to know what changed is asking somebody to choose\nblind. The entries are Unreleased rather than numbered — the bump belongs to\nwhoever cuts the release, not to this commit.\n\nTests hold the pieces in step: the pipe''s image tag is this package''s own\nversion, the baked CLI is the version each package defaults to, and a\nchangelog describes either the current version or what a bump would carry.\n\nAlso raised the script suites'' timeout. They spawn a real shell and a real\nnode per case and sat close enough to the 5s default that the workspace\nrunning suites in parallel tipped one over — which showed up as a failure in\nan unrelated change, and would have again.","tree":{"sha":"bb1e907e08e86bcc92658729e645bf9c771c85e7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/bb1e907e08e86bcc92658729e645bf9c771c85e7"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/20236ead1faeee35c28c70ec9ab52a91716aab65","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/20236ead1faeee35c28c70ec9ab52a91716aab65","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKDIwMjM2ZWFkMWZhZWVlMzVjMjhjNzBlYzlhYjUyYTkxNzE2YWFiNjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/824a76e75465213af28d0bce598e106a61fdf91b","sha":"824a76e75465213af28d0bce598e106a61fdf91b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/824a76e75465213af28d0bce598e106a61fdf91b"}],"sha":"20236ead1faeee35c28c70ec9ab52a91716aab65","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/20236ead1faeee35c28c70ec9ab52a91716aab65"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/824a76e75465213af28d0bce598e106a61fdf91b/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:59:55Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T07:00:05Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"📦 fix(gitlab,bitbucket): stops fetching the CLI into the customer''s CI on every run\n\nBoth CI paths ran `npx --yes @coldtea/pr-lens-cli@<version>` at job time, so\nevery pipeline downloaded and executed whatever the registry served that\nminute — inside a job holding the project''s CI/CD variables, with the\ninstall time billed to the project, and the whole run depending on npm being\nup.\n\nThe Bitbucket pipe is already a versioned image, so there was no reason for\nit: the CLI is baked in at build time now, pinned to the version the\nmetadata declares, and a test holds those two in step so the image cannot\nship built against one version while defaulting to another.\n\nThe component''s image is the consumer''s choice, so it ships a Dockerfile for\none with the CLI installed and documents pointing `image` at it. On a plain\nnode image nothing is baked and the npx path still runs — that absence is\nwhat selects it, which is why the guard tolerates the variable being unset.\n\nEither way the script prefers a baked CLI only when it is the version asked\nfor, so overriding `cli_version` still works.","tree":{"sha":"43e0d1d8b135d7a54bb20281a8d92d09fa6bdc0a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/43e0d1d8b135d7a54bb20281a8d92d09fa6bdc0a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/824a76e75465213af28d0bce598e106a61fdf91b","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/824a76e75465213af28d0bce598e106a61fdf91b","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKDgyNGE3NmU3NTQ2NTIxM2FmMjhkMGJjZTU5OGUxMDZhNjFmZGY5MWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/09045688f86d29eb423a40fb237884f80b2019b5","sha":"09045688f86d29eb423a40fb237884f80b2019b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/09045688f86d29eb423a40fb237884f80b2019b5"}],"sha":"824a76e75465213af28d0bce598e106a61fdf91b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/824a76e75465213af28d0bce598e106a61fdf91b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/09045688f86d29eb423a40fb237884f80b2019b5/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:56:03Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:56:03Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"🎨 fix(gitlab,bitbucket): stops handing dark-mode readers a light diagram\n\nGitLab and Bitbucket both show one image and cannot swap on the reader''s\ntheme, and the composer picked that image with `pair.light ?? pair.dark` —\nso every dark-mode reader on either forge got a glaring white rectangle with\nstrokes tuned for a ground they were not looking at. For a product whose\nentire output is the diagram, that is most of the product.\n\nA transparent render does not fix it, and the arithmetic is why: for a flat\ncolour, contrast against white is 1.05/(L+0.05) and against black is\n(L+0.05)/0.05, equal only at L ≈ 0.179 where both are 4.58:1 — barely over\nAA at best, and under it against a near-black page like #0d1117. Text cannot\nsit directly on both pages and stay readable.\n\nSo there is a third render, `neutral`, which is opaque and self-contained:\nit brings its own dimmed ground, every ratio inside it is fixed wherever it\nlands, and its border keeps an edge against a light page and a dark one. On\na dark page it sits naturally; on a light one it reads as a deliberately\ndark figure, the way a screenshot does.\n\n`neutral` replaces the pair rather than joining it — a surface wants the\npair or the single image, never all three — so MAX_VIEWS stays bound to\nTHEME_PAIR. Binding it to the size of the enum would have shrunk the view\ncap for a theme no render asks for alongside the others, and 256/3 is not a\nwhole number of views.\n\n`CommentSurface.themePair: boolean` becomes `themeStrategy: \"pair\" |\n\"neutral\"`, which is the decision the composer was making with a `??`. The\nGitLab component and the Bitbucket pipe now render `--theme neutral`.\n\nA manifest with only the pair still produces a diagram on a single-image\nsurface, so an older render keeps working — that path is a fallback now\nrather than the intent, and says so.\n\nTests: contrast is computed rather than eyeballed — body text clears AA\nagainst its own ground in all three palettes, and the neutral panel stays\nvisible against both pages. Per-forge tests pin which asset each comment\npoints at. Mutation-verified: putting GitLab back on the pair strategy fails\nthree of them.","tree":{"sha":"ec7503cf8b3e1bb96682fcb72fde06c41ddfc1c4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/ec7503cf8b3e1bb96682fcb72fde06c41ddfc1c4"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/09045688f86d29eb423a40fb237884f80b2019b5","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/09045688f86d29eb423a40fb237884f80b2019b5","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKDA5MDQ1Njg4Zjg2ZDI5ZWI0MjNhNDBmYjIzNzg4NGY4MGIyMDE5YjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/e1179fc2aedd23cf1e3b190b308f8fd4e22de68c","sha":"e1179fc2aedd23cf1e3b190b308f8fd4e22de68c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/e1179fc2aedd23cf1e3b190b308f8fd4e22de68c"}],"sha":"09045688f86d29eb423a40fb237884f80b2019b5","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/09045688f86d29eb423a40fb237884f80b2019b5"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/e1179fc2aedd23cf1e3b190b308f8fd4e22de68c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:46:11Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-21T06:46:11Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"🔧 fix(bitbucket,gitlab): makes the pipe listable and the component safe to include\n\n**The Pipe could not be published.** pipe.yml had `maintainer` and `vendor`\nas plain strings where Atlassian''s metadata spec wants objects with a name\nand a website, and it was missing `category`, which is required and drawn\nfrom a fixed set. Atlassian validates this on submission, so the pipe worked\nfor anyone who already knew the image name and was invisible to everyone\nelse — which defeats shipping a pipe rather than a raw script block. Fixed\nagainst the published spec, with `Code quality` spelled their way, and the\nREADME reordered into the headings they mandate.\n\n**A PR Lens failure failed the consumer''s pipeline.** The component set no\n`allow_failure`, no `timeout` and no `retry`, so a transient API error or a\nrate limit turned into a red merge request whose code was fine, and a hung\nmodel call ran until the project''s global timeout on the customer''s CI\nminutes. It now allows failure by default — this draws a picture, it does\nnot judge the code — bounds its own runtime, retries only transient runner\nand API classes, and is interruptible so a superseded pipeline stops drawing\na commit nobody is looking at.\n\n**Inputs were untyped and the job was not composable.** Every input now\ndeclares a type, and the ones with a closed set declare `options` or a\n`regex`, so `provider: maybe` or a malformed version is refused when the\npipeline is created rather than failing inside a shell comparison three\nsteps later. The job name is an input, so the component can appear twice in\none pipeline instead of colliding with itself.\n\n`branding` and `comment` stay strings with `options` rather than becoming\nbooleans: a pipeline passing `\"true\"` today keeps working.\n\nThe render is now a job artifact, which needed the work directory inside\n`CI_PROJECT_DIR` — the script gained an `mkdir -p`, applied to both copies\nso the byte-for-byte lockstep with scripts/lens.sh holds.\n\nTests: the pipe metadata is held to the shape Atlassian validates, the\nREADME to their heading order, and the component to allow-failure,\ntransient-only retries, and an artifact path that matches where the script\nactually writes. Mutation-verified — a string maintainer, a missing\ncategory, `script_failure` in the retry set, a flipped allow_failure default\nand a mismatched artifact path each fail the test that covers them.","tree":{"sha":"70a6ac3c8d9af50c81869d0b945da136662e07fe","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/trees/70a6ac3c8d9af50c81869d0b945da136662e07fe"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/git/commits/e1179fc2aedd23cf1e3b190b308f8fd4e22de68c","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/e1179fc2aedd23cf1e3b190b308f8fd4e22de68c","node_id":"C_kwDOT-8RJNoAKGUxMTc5ZmMyYWVkZDIzY2YxZTNiMTkwYjMwOGY4ZmQ0ZTIyZGU2OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commit/d4fcf594e8787faa1eed55c42d35ab46d51a4677","sha":"d4fcf594e8787faa1eed55c42d35ab46d51a4677","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/d4fcf594e8787faa1eed55c42d35ab46d51a4677"}],"sha":"e1179fc2aedd23cf1e3b190b308f8fd4e22de68c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/e1179fc2aedd23cf1e3b190b308f8fd4e22de68c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/46670083?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/ohansFavour","id":46670083,"login":"ohansFavour","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ2NjcwMDgz","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/ohansFavour","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/coldteadotai/pr-lens/commits/d4fcf594e8787faa1eed55c42d35ab46d51a4677/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-20T19:03:07Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-20T19:03:07Z","email":"fohanekwu@gmail.com","name":"Favour Ohans"},"message":"