/users/gonzalomenghi/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/gonzalomenghi","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gonzalomenghi/inventario-hogar/commits/1143cc3598cc545a557962437ca145432f416e55/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:02:48Z","email":"gmenghi40@gmail.com","name":"Gonzalo Menghi"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-24T20:02:48Z","email":"gmenghi40@gmail.com","name":"Gonzalo Menghi"},"message":"Sync catalogo_sepa_ref from real SEPA/Precios Claros data\n\nReplaces the unimplemented Edge Function stub with a GitHub Actions\ncron job: the national dataset is 300MB+ compressed and one comercio\nalone has 4M+ product rows, well past what a Supabase Edge Function\n(short execution/memory limits) can handle. Downloads the day''s ZIP,\nstreams productos.csv per comercio through unzip+readline (never\nbuffers the full CSV), and upserts distinct EAN products in batches.\n\nScoped to 5 chosen comercios (Carrefour, DIA, SuperChangomas, La\nAnonima, Mariano Max) rather than all 18 - covers most of what people\nactually buy without parsing tens of millions of extra rows. No\ncategory mapping attempted (SEPA doesn''t share our taxonomy).\n\nVerified end-to-end against local Supabase with a real run: 11.4M\nrows read, 62,831 unique EAN products upserted, buscar_producto_similar\nreturning real matches against the synced catalog.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f082e64c16664acdf8f23a0d936830f0232c6859","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gonzalomenghi/inventario-hogar/git/trees/f082e64c16664acdf8f23a0d936830f0232c6859"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/gonzalomenghi/inventario-hogar/git/commits/1143cc3598cc545a557962437ca145432f416e55","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96753378?v=4","events_url":"https://a