url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/robertSt7","id":104770750,"login":"robertSt7","node_id":"U_kgDOBj6svg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/commits/5eaf29da0b4d3425eab1c63ff289dd0dbe3bf685/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:32:46Z","email":"104770750+robertSt7@users.noreply.github.com","name":"robertSt7"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T14:32:46Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Replace the template placeholder docs with real ones (#23)\n\n* Replace the template placeholder docs with real ones\n\nREADME and the installation page still read \"x Template x\" / \"xTemplate\nBundlex\" from the bundle skeleton the repo started from. They, and the\none page that did exist, are replaced with documentation of what the\nbundle actually does: the toolbar, linking and dropping elements from the\ntree, the numbered-list display, and the stored value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Correct compatibility, undo scope, and stored-value wording\n\n- The README implied images could be inserted by URL too; only a link\n  can be.\n- The installation page said only \"version 2026\", looser than what\n  composer.json actually requires.\n- The undo table row claimed every toolbar edit is undoable; applying\n  the code view writes through directly and is not.\n- The stored-value note for data objects said what is edited is what is\n  saved, contradicting the sanitizer and rewriting described just above\n  it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Correct the blockquote toggle claim and the image-size condition\n\n- Blockquote applies formatBlock unconditionally; a second click does\n  not restore a paragraph the way the list buttons do.\n- The image-drop rule omitted two conditions from the actual check: the\n  original is kept only under 600px and in a browser-native format,\n  otherwise a generated thumbnail is used regardless of size.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"77ac53d6a1ffdf3c5246e7fe17191eab6319f38b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/git/trees/77ac53d6a1ffdf3c5246e7fe17191eab6319f38b"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/git/commits/5eaf29da0b4d3425eab1c63ff289dd0dbe3bf685","verification":{"payload":"tree 77ac53d6a1ffdf3c5246e7fe17191eab6319f38b\nparent 2d977f067c4b2909ab07d5c2528acf948ef6968d\nauthor robertSt7 <104770750+robertSt7@users.noreply.github.com> 1789137166 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789137166 +0200\n\nReplace the template placeholder docs with real ones (#23)\n\n* Replace the template placeholder docs with real ones\n\nREADME and the installation page still read \"x Template x\" / \"xTemplate\nBundlex\" from the bundle skeleton the repo started from. They, and the\none page that did exist, are replaced with documentation of what the\nbundle actually does: the toolbar, linking and dropping elements from the\ntree, the numbered-list display, and the stored value.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Correct compatibility, undo scope, and stored-value wording\n\n- The README implied images could be inserted by URL too; only a link\n  can be.\n- The installation page said only \"version 2026\", looser than what\n  composer.json actually requires.\n- The undo table row claimed every toolbar edit is undoable; applying\n  the code view writes through directly and is not.\n- The stored-value note for data objects said what is edited is what is\n  saved, contradicting the sanitizer and rewriting described just above\n  it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Correct the blockquote toggle claim and the image-size condition\n\n- Blockquote applies formatBlock unconditionally; a second click does\n  not restore a paragraph the way the list buttons do.\n- The image-drop rule omitted two conditions from the actual check: the\n  original is kept only under 600px and in a browser-native format,\n  otherwise a generated thumbnail is used regardless of size.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpBEOCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAzIkQAK7KDc1z0PjOjpcDgJAhxHfT\njfub/flxNH1GfXGBkLbm3feU24LAgnFM4+c810vIxVtcOD/lImDvarsP5JCaFXnX\nEop2TcovJK7VyAjwSx9AVjEyEaW5qinA1+4BpSyAGUbrf9M5iS6M4Ie4T0mD/t+o\nQTnXTUXFYarpvgMxswVaInNEkjOZy1vAmMLeTFTULpfN+AEBY6+aqfrBdTulIN+7\nGSpmn+P7BC5N0Clg8qdxIcozlCtrwfI0SSqHcGxIyeCPRiLdM585Au+JACRF50lQ\nnk/sCVqygLbgQjjxiGzylYpfrqX05FxxqltBl3R8Ptt86LQjDWyaHlom0hfNMjLT\nV9g+pfDOJ84EN96tAXKU4W2LKN8WlkSLwF75iuPtzzmju97XWYaRarSxn7rWHrBH\nYQXe3OFudXBxvUrE1HFNy7KKCRu+KHVQL8wAptW85VBNa/SAsEKyRb6aXS7R1Ygh\ndnMoPnPipMvMiwhrn8yd2hrShFT6PTysxsFzZXcs5RWDnYRG+znPLWARYS1DtiJI\n+8L/BHzjqsENb24ZK+SF5D0Pk2hqA2tgADc/z95KgtofNUDGVEsHe3c3Ybi8mffe\nEAUs1NenpNRFB2ithtT9LCNqS13JsWMpnzZAdHXp2N31eoqLjDNjxbQN52lOvTJB\nfFSXRBecPzhaA/tDZL/a\n=5XMD\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T14:32:47Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-f