T_fY69oAKDJkOTc3ZjA2N2M0YjI5MDlhYjA3ZDVjMjUyOGFjZjk0OGVmNjk2OGQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/commit/ba97ded13a45542e81a1f677b069de7c0497c8a7","sha":"ba97ded13a45542e81a1f677b069de7c0497c8a7","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/commits/ba97ded13a45542e81a1f677b069de7c0497c8a7"}],"sha":"2d977f067c4b2909ab07d5c2528acf948ef6968d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/commits/2d977f067c4b2909ab07d5c2528acf948ef6968d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/104770750?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/robertSt7","id":104770750,"login":"robertSt7","node_id":"U_kgDOBj6svg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/robertSt7","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/commits/ba97ded13a45542e81a1f677b069de7c0497c8a7/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:57:37Z","email":"104770750+robertSt7@users.noreply.github.com","name":"robertSt7"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:57:37Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"Let the link popover change the link the caret sits in (#17)\n\n* Let the link popover change the link the caret sits in\n\nOpening the popover inside a link used to offer an empty URL field and\n\"Insert\", so the only way to change an address was the source view. The\nselection now reports the link under the caret, the popover starts from its\nURL and updates it in place through the undo history. The element\nattributes go with the old address, as Pimcore would otherwise rewrite the\nnew URL back to that element''s path on output.\n\nThe popover''s action button now sits at the right.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Only edit a link the whole selection sits in\n\nA selection starting inside a link and running past it is text the user\nis picking to link, not that link. It was reported as the link under the\ncaret, so the popover offered to update the first link and rewrote it\nwholesale. One shared predicate now decides what counts as inside a link,\nfor the toolbar state and the update alike.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Keep an unchanged link as it is, and ignore a caret placed before one\n\nConfirming a link''s address unchanged rewrote the tag and, with it,\ndropped the element attributes Pimcore tracks the reference by; it is now\na no-op. And the link lookup went through the child at the range''s offset,\nso a caret sitting just before a link counted as inside it and offered to\nupdate a link the caret was not in; it now starts from the range''s own\ncontainer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add a regression test for the link update''s undo step\n\nThe existing test only checked the value emitted right after an update,\nso a change that mutated the link without going through the undo history\nwould still pass. The stub''s execCommand now keeps a snapshot per\nmutating command and restores one on undo, and a test drives that path\nend to end: update a link, undo, and check the original href and\nPimcore attributes are back.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Expose the link button''s active state to assistive technology\n\nIt gained a visual active state when the caret sits in a link, but unlike\nthe toolbar''s other stateful controls carried no aria-pressed, so a\nscreen-reader user had no way to tell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"d14f1c4594319daa219585841bea03d9e682d70a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/git/trees/d14f1c4594319daa219585841bea03d9e682d70a"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/pimcore/pimcore-wysiwyg-editor/git/commits/ba97ded13a45542e81a1f677b069de7c0497c8a7","verification":{"payload":"tree d14f1c4594319daa219585841bea03d9e682d70a\nparent a0863da6733fd7bd5edc5e39142300ca1c4712d4\nauthor robertSt7 <104770750+robertSt7@users.noreply.github.com> 1789131457 +0200\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789131457 +0200\n\nLet the link popover change the link the caret sits in (#17)\n\n* Let the link popover change the link the caret sits in\n\nOpening the popover inside a link used to offer an empty URL field and\n\"Insert\", so the only way to change an address was the source view. The\nselection now reports the link under the caret, the popover starts from its\nURL and updates it in place through the undo history. The element\nattributes go with the old address, as Pimcore would otherwise rewrite the\nnew URL back to that element''s path on output.\n\nThe popover''s action button now sits at the right.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Only edit a link the whole selection sits in\n\nA selection starting inside a link and running past it is text the user\nis picking to link, not that link. It was reported as the link under the\ncaret, so the popover offered to update the first link and rewrote it\nwholesale. One shared predicate now decides what counts as inside a link,\nfor the toolbar state and the update alike.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Keep an unchanged link as it is, and ignore a caret placed before one\n\nConfirming a link''s address unchanged rewrote the tag and, with it,\ndropped the element attributes Pimcore tracks the reference by; it is now\na no-op. And the link lookup went through the child at the range''s offset,\nso a caret sitting just before a link counted as inside it and offered to\nupdate a link the caret was not in; it now starts from the range''s own\ncontainer.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Add a regression test for the link update''s undo step\n\nThe existing test only checked the value emitted right after an update,\nso a change that mutated the link without going through the undo history\nwould still pass. The stub''s execCommand now keeps a snapshot per\nmutating command and restores one on undo, and a test drives that path\nend to end: update a link, undo, and check the original href and\nPimcore attributes are back.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* Expose the link button''s active state to assistive technology\n\nIt gained a visual active state when the caret sits in a link, but unlike\nthe toolbar''s other stateful controls carried no aria-pressed, so a\nscreen-reader user had no way to tell.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo/rBCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAyDwQAIE8iZ88db60sVe0gQVoRsOv\nXSPKVpl+OJv4Pzb+B9MQNbbwrMJyPyPqR5tCd9mnu8tmd9rlIhT+oFHVzMPpVwfG\nE0Nn1uK5y19opBqJKTAsq2lGnkwRCiCIXxSa34VFkiP2mykV6g+eVxSvuznNLt1A\ntUE180HAI//1K6xVVpjsAYmyYGG69UpsdcLIXXXu8DmPm5wGDJssBB0xLC3rNVgw\nqnZM9ryTx/UGTrjA03RjCLBuRBnUb318iuMFZ6LyDzP2fywsIEc2Eh1PqeM8EYkD\nNpwVNDL7vKRGUyd9GoT3mIvWqgNpmp24hzbmcxCp0h9BbFOYIFlytSdBp32x/n+2\nFJi70IC5fzvfLrd+NF8/PR0PrsFP7t+QY9N8hql4vT2JT8sN1b1Lzj2rLkhwxwwz\n40q1TODsZAlQrtY6h2PrnXA0kJvLf9gEH