ic.com>\n\n* fix: refuse a deployed MCP surface nobody addressed, and say who sees the 401\n\nReview of #47 found both halves of the same mistake: a document served\nwith a 200 that names something no client can reach, and a README that\ntold the reader the runtime''s own 401 is what starts a client''s OAuth\nflow.\n\nThe refusal (F2). In a deployed runtime context — the same signal that\nalready refuses a loopback SELF_UPSTREAM or PUBLIC_URL — an unset\nMCP_PUBLIC_URL leaves the resource identifier reconstructed from the\nforwarded headers, missing the route prefix the gateway strips and\ncarrying the hop''s scheme rather than the client''s, and an unset\nHOST_ISSUER_URL publishes the in-cluster address this composition dials\nthe host at as the authorization server. Both were served from a solution\nthat registered and looked healthy, with one boot log line as the only\nsignal. Now the boot is refused, naming the variable that fixes each; a\nlocal run resolves a host it can actually reach and is untouched. Pinned\nby a test, confirmed by deleting the refusal and watching it go red.\n\nWho sees the challenge (F1). The gateway strips identity headers and runs\next_authz before proxying, so an unauthenticated MCP request is denied\nthere and never reaches the solution: the runtime''s 401 is the direct and\nlocal caller''s answer, and the shape the gateway''s own challenge has to\nmatch. Emitting it there is codefly-dev/module-saas-starter#1003. The\nREADME said otherwise in the one place a reader would check, which is\nworse than silence — it sends whoever is debugging discovery to the wrong\nrepository. The metadata document is still served here: it is what that\nchallenge has to name.\n\nFour smaller ones from the same review. A forwarded proto is accepted\nonly as http or https, so \"javascript\" cannot be spliced in front of\n\"://\" in a URL handed to a client (F3). The no-session 403 names the kind\nthe gateway actually stamped instead of asserting api_key, which sent a\ncaller of another kind looking for an API key it does not have (F4). A\ntool call logs its name — the one thing the accounts mint audit cannot\nreconstruct — and neither its arguments nor any credential (F6). And both\ncollisions are refused at boot by name rather than panicking inside\nServeMux after the listener is open, or silently keeping the last of two\nServeMCP calls and serving none of the first''s tools (F7).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqwaOICRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAaU8QAFf8kqj9x0CG72qU+4pxksRC\nswuPSohDwzXij2Hns3BJGElIyUMH0BwjCCdQUs//RwlR/2REU/PoVLkscGUz3eQ5\nHa9y5IMAQJSN6XG0B4547M8TFb4jUXE7kkYdOrLwntZvEs1kZgzOk8HkZXqOaqak\nwZoxx+FwJx6Y3u0o/HwAFgvG51Y7TtCpm9ckfqf7RRYYOuKXOO6YDQ1VSI5xpje9\neh+Zqat+xk6fyuYx6NQJMhgiLy63S4zx0pj/9+60lBspe0wu0XEGGJcnoAGOwBH+\n03C+bntrSkhojGcMmWG9FMMZYGZQNH5whsTsGNK/bnpnMUMPp4nUxnNTyAGZrjD4\nxgU4uD3Zmr0h8GvXXBmJicDEI5kEAK7U9f4u3e6z1B5Llw4ytr3aKIl9JcBaf7gg\ntzsH7gGaTqjl96bIOHRudko/1f9ccLvTgs6+kGycJYnHoSGTj6kBOP8DmijVXOjl\nAex+AXKjhP62IGBAMQrSe2JkC95Dy5+zylNHO2ndXdmZKgwXDNqY0zR5iZHV2cUM\nFdHjMigzWJzkPjCMvmYc2hNLv6LzlqrtwrDrLEyASp0a+G1IUJ5fZyNvT/a05Lfz\njBMUFKzYKo/QxMVD+c3oCiJ2kwwqyo2scUPImfdKY4iNH9m2rwGGz48sfLS/9+tJ\n9tbdu+LDKCsdWYcMvxoP\n=aX6f\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-10-04T00:53:29Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/d727d73c2867819a19ff8e59f45e69d5911fbeeb","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKGQ3MjdkNzNjMjg2NzgxOWExOWZmOGU1OWY0NWU2OWQ1OTExZmJlZWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/8da58cd4a6033579f563c508826c6d2f9f147406","sha":"8da58cd4a6033579f563c508826c6d2f9f147406","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/8da58cd4a6033579f563c508826c6d2f9f147406"}],"sha":"d727d73c2867819a19ff8e59f45e69d5911fbeeb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/d727d73c2867819a19ff8e59f45e69d5911fbeeb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/8da58cd4a6033579f563c508826c6d2f9f147406/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:26:33Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T23:26:33Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"message":"feat: passthroughtest, a seam to run the consumed-module passthrough in a test\n\nA consuming solution could not exercise its page''s calls to a consumed\nmodule in a test: the passthrough handler is internal, and Serve resolves\nthe gateway and api.consumes from the composition and registers with the\nhost. A `codefly test` suite therefore could not drive a streamed method at\nall.\n\nServer.PassthroughHandler(PassthroughEnvironment) builds the passthrough\nexactly as Serve does: the same boot check (validatePassthrough) and the\nsame mounting code, now one function (mountPassthrough) that serve and the\nseam both call, against a gateway URL and api.consumes projection the\ncaller supplies. Nothing else of the solution is served and nothing\nregisters.\n\nPackage passthroughtest builds on it: a fake host gateway that mints the\nviewer''s Work Context and forwards /v1/<as>/* to the test''s own module\nserver (streams flushed as they arrive, cancellation propagated), hooks to\nroute a module and to refuse mints, a record of every mint and of every\nforwarded call with the mint it presented, and a client that calls as a\nviewer with the identity headers the gateway stamps.\n\nIts own tests drive a unary call, a stream of several messages, per-method\nauthority, the response field mask on both, and cancellation reaching the\nmodule when the page disconnects, and a refused mint refusing only its\nmethod. The formatting gate now covers the whole tree, not only ./*.go.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"34f6a756d03f5b01627eae3f4cc8e8139419bd59","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/34f6a756d03f5b01627eae3f4cc8e8139419bd59"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/8da58cd4a6033579f563c508826c6d2f9f147406","verification":{"payload":"tree 34f6a756d03f5b01627eae3f4cc8e8139419bd59\nparent cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790465193 -0400\ncommitter antoinetoussaint-byte <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790465193 -0400\n\nfeat: passthroughtest, a seam to run the consumed-module passthrough in a test\n\nA consuming solution could not exercise its page''s calls to a consumed\nmodule in a test: the passthrough handler is internal, and Serve resolves\nthe gateway and api.consumes from the composition and registers with the\nhost. A `codefly test` suite therefore could not drive a streamed method at\nall.\n\nServer.PassthroughHandler(PassthroughEnvironment) builds the passthrough\nexactly as Serve does: the same boot check (validatePassthrough) and the\nsame mounting code, now one function (mountPassthrough) that serve and the\nseam both call, against a gateway URL and api.consumes projection the\ncaller supplies. Nothing else of the solution is served and nothing\nregisters.\n\nPackage passthroughtest builds on it: a fake host gateway that mints the\nviewer''s Work Context and forwards /v1/<as>/* to the test''s own module\nserver (streams flushed as they arrive, cancellation propagated), hooks to\nroute a module and to refuse mints, a record of every mint and of every\nforwarded call with the mint it presented, and a client that calls as a\nviewer with the identity headers the gateway stamps.\n\nIts own tests drive a unary call, a stream of several messages, per-method\nauthority, the response field mask on both, and cancellation reaching the\nmodule when the page disconnects, and a refused mint refusing only its\nmethod. The formatting gate now covers the whole tree, not only ./*.go.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcdDfnJkwhq+GcBoTN3TX56bX0H\n8InRU9/eZzzo1eEkwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQH2XWztIFyQOasrG8cLuqDp8T165nI2OifVWPXRtgu5LwZD0wtSahv++G8VKS6hRiY\nmyfT3CkwZQbMSXyiIk9gY=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T23:27:03Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/8da58cd4a6033579f563c508826c6d2f9f147406","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDhkYTU4Y2Q0YTYwMzM1NzlmNTYzYzUwODgyNmM2ZDJmOWYxNDc0MDY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0","sha":"cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0"}],"sha":"8da58cd4a6033579f563c508826c6d2f9f147406","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/8da58cd4a6033579f563c508826c6d2f9f147406"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:30:51Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T22:30:51Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"message":"feat: pass a consumed module''s server-streaming methods through to the page\n\nThe passthrough refused every streaming method (\"only unary methods pass\nthrough\"), so a page could not follow a module''s live state. A\nserver-streaming method is now served as a Connect server-streaming\nprocedure at the same /modules/<as>/<pkg.Service>/<Method> path, under\nexactly the unary rules:\n\n- the authority minted for that method (or the bearer alone, for a\n  ViewerBearer module);\n- the declared response fields applied to every streamed message.\n\nBoth bounds are declared per method: MaxStreamDuration (default 5 min, at\nmost 30 min; the stream then ends with deadline_exceeded) and\nMaxStreamMessageBytes (default 1 MiB; a larger message ends the stream with\nresource_exhausted and is never truncated). The page disconnecting cancels\nthe module request. Client-streaming methods, and stream bounds on a unary\nmethod or out of range, are refused at boot.\n\nA module answers a streamed method over its google.api.http binding with\ngrpc-gateway''s server-streaming wire: newline-delimited JSON,\n{\"result\": …} or {\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\"}} per line\n(application/x-ndjson, or application/json). Gateway.TranscodedStream is the\nsame call for a solution handler. The interface artifact marks a streamed\noperation (x-streaming: server).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cd6b54de68f8cb30d7a0958f00defc58f6746619","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/cd6b54de68f8cb30d7a0958f00defc58f6746619"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0","verification":{"payload":"tree cd6b54de68f8cb30d7a0958f00defc58f6746619\nparent ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d\nauthor Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790461851 -0400\ncommitter Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790461851 -0400\n\nfeat: pass a consumed module''s server-streaming methods through to the page\n\nThe passthrough refused every streaming method (\"only unary methods pass\nthrough\"), so a page could not follow a module''s live state. A\nserver-streaming method is now served as a Connect server-streaming\nprocedure at the same /modules/<as>/<pkg.Service>/<Method> path, under\nexactly the unary rules:\n\n- the authority minted for that method (or the bearer alone, for a\n  ViewerBearer module);\n- the declared response fields applied to every streamed message.\n\nBoth bounds are declared per method: MaxStreamDuration (default 5 min, at\nmost 30 min; the stream then ends with deadline_exceeded) and\nMaxStreamMessageBytes (default 1 MiB; a larger message ends the stream with\nresource_exhausted and is never truncated). The page disconnecting cancels\nthe module request. Client-streaming methods, and stream bounds on a unary\nmethod or out of range, are refused at boot.\n\nA module answers a streamed method over its google.api.http binding with\ngrpc-gateway''s server-streaming wire: newline-delimited JSON,\n{\"result\": …} or {\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\"}} per line\n(application/x-ndjson, or application/json). Gateway.TranscodedStream is the\nsame call for a solution handler. The interface artifact marks a streamed\noperation (x-streaming: server).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcdDfnJkwhq+GcBoTN3TX56bX0H\n8InRU9/eZzzo1eEkwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQHn6xS2hoIvMAZqdcpG2BgRPPRDcjUWfw8QvwromhMFaLa6S8IoPvcVOh0BFRZXuXy\nlEKLClnH3W+Ch7BDHh3gA=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T22:30:53Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKGNjZTI1NTk3NjBlM2QzYmE4MTg5NzY2OTg3MTM4ZDVlNDQ2MWVhYjA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d","sha":"ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d"}],"sha":"cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/cce2559760e3d3ba8189766987138d5e4461eab0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:53:03Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-26T19:53:03Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"message":"feat: mint the viewer''s authority per consumed method, not per module\n\nA consumed method may declare its own Scopes, which replace the module''s for a\ncall to that method. One module''s methods that need different authority are\ndeclared under one `as`, and each call mints only its own method''s scopes, so\na viewer who lacks one method''s authority is refused that method as\npermission_denied (with the issuer''s reason, naming the permission) and is\nstill served the others. Declarations that could never mint are refused at\nboot. A mint refusal is now a typed WorkContextRefusal that still unwraps to\nthe GatewayError it was.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a0df157c17991e459bad363db58dff482d5fda3c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/a0df157c17991e459bad363db58dff482d5fda3c"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d","verification":{"payload":"tree a0df157c17991e459bad363db58dff482d5fda3c\nparent 8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0\nauthor Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790452383 -0400\ncommitter Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790452383 -0400\n\nfeat: mint the viewer''s authority per consumed method, not per module\n\nA consumed method may declare its own Scopes, which replace the module''s for a\ncall to that method. One module''s methods that need different authority are\ndeclared under one `as`, and each call mints only its own method''s scopes, so\na viewer who lacks one method''s authority is refused that method as\npermission_denied (with the issuer''s reason, naming the permission) and is\nstill served the others. Declarations that could never mint are refused at\nboot. A mint refusal is now a typed WorkContextRefusal that still unwraps to\nthe GatewayError it was.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcdDfnJkwhq+GcBoTN3TX56bX0H\n8InRU9/eZzzo1eEkwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQNCgFNLi0+R2J8awdxZuUi9IViK/2Rx5bs08IPK/eaJROirQUBoaDLOBBhi+GnZsGq\nNAMXlVs+gVUJAIufe9sgU=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-26T19:53:05Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKGNhMmZhYzEzYTc1MTllOTZiYjNlMmI3ODEyZDVkZjU3OTI4YTlkOWQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0","sha":"8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0"}],"sha":"ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/ca2fac13a7519e96bb3e2b7812d5df57928a9d9d"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:35:31Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T16:35:31Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"message":"feat: render a backend''s interface artifact from its declaration and manifest version\n\nEvery solution rendered its interface artifact the same way: read the\nversion from service.codefly.yaml, then render its operations. A solution\nwhose page calls consumed modules also added the passthrough declaration.\nInterfaceArtifact does this in one call, and ServiceVersion reads the\nmanifest''s version, so the artifact carries the version the platform ships.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"eb6acadda779087e8fe6b6f2196d8ca90de4dbf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/eb6acadda779087e8fe6b6f2196d8ca90de4dbf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0","verification":{"payload":"tree eb6acadda779087e8fe6b6f2196d8ca90de4dbf6\nparent 2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43\nauthor Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790354131 -0400\ncommitter Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790354131 -0400\n\nfeat: render a backend''s interface artifact from its declaration and manifest version\n\nEvery solution rendered its interface artifact the same way: read the\nversion from service.codefly.yaml, then render its operations. A solution\nwhose page calls consumed modules also added the passthrough declaration.\nInterfaceArtifact does this in one call, and ServiceVersion reads the\nmanifest''s version, so the artifact carries the version the platform ships.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcdDfnJkwhq+GcBoTN3TX56bX0H\n8InRU9/eZzzo1eEkwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQMY/Ws2hrdPlBx9f/P0Ib5wHzeU9zLtC/pmDi8BIOAyKUq5EPJ/3VE/lKsfH6tswUd\nC7vtV2luQX+koiAotxGg4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T16:35:32Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDhlYTJjY2E2ZWVlYjBhYWQzNmZhZjJkMWU5MTE2OGY3YjMyZGM3ZDA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43","sha":"2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43"}],"sha":"8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/8ea2cca6eeeb0aad36faf2d1e91168f7b32dc7d0"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:37:15Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:37:15Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"message":"feat: pin part of a passthrough request server-side\n\nA solution sometimes fixes part of what its page may ask a module: a filter\nclause selecting the collection an installation serves, say. Without a way\nto say so in the declaration, that is a relay handler again. ConsumedMethod.Pin\nis merged into every request before it is forwarded (proto.Merge), so a\npinned scalar replaces the page''s value and a pinned repeated value is added\nto the page''s: a clause the module ANDs stays in force whatever the page sends.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"a050a26398544f83fabbca715908e48eb7c61243","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/a050a26398544f83fabbca715908e48eb7c61243"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43","verification":{"payload":"tree a050a26398544f83fabbca715908e48eb7c61243\nparent 001880b1541f410f7b4a622e1383d720b960d001\nauthor Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790350635 -0400\ncommitter Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790350635 -0400\n\nfeat: pin part of a passthrough request server-side\n\nA solution sometimes fixes part of what its page may ask a module: a filter\nclause selecting the collection an installation serves, say. Without a way\nto say so in the declaration, that is a relay handler again. ConsumedMethod.Pin\nis merged into every request before it is forwarded (proto.Merge), so a\npinned scalar replaces the page''s value and a pinned repeated value is added\nto the page''s: a clause the module ANDs stays in force whatever the page sends.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcdDfnJkwhq+GcBoTN3TX56bX0H\n8InRU9/eZzzo1eEkwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQE3moYHqCJXZnNxUOqstv3cSJ8wXHGMwXQNuczCpEZHZfqxEwiHM3gD9eRWiDrCSn+\nZnXhTk6DJEpYqz85TcZAE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:37:17Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDJjMmEyZjQ2MGVkNGRjNjI2ZDVjMjc4ZGJjZTY0YjZhYzRjNDJmNDM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/001880b1541f410f7b4a622e1383d720b960d001","sha":"001880b1541f410f7b4a622e1383d720b960d001","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/001880b1541f410f7b4a622e1383d720b960d001"}],"sha":"2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/2c2a2f460ed4dc626d5c278dbce64b6ac4c42f43"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/001880b1541f410f7b4a622e1383d720b960d001/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:31:37Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T15:31:37Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"message":"feat: let a solution''s page call a consumed module''s declared operations\n\nA page reaches only its solution''s own backend, so every module read it made\nneeded a handler in the solution that decoded the request, minted the\nviewer''s capability, called the module and re-encoded the answer: the same\nrelay in every solution, once per operation.\n\nServer.Consumes declares instead which operations of which consumed module\nthe page may call. Each is served as a Connect unary procedure at\n/modules/<as>/<package.Service>/<Method>, so the module''s generated client is\nused unmodified. A call is answered by the module as the viewer: the runtime\nmints the declared Work Context (ForModule), or forwards only the bearer to a\nmodule that authenticates the viewer itself, and forwards the request over\nthe method''s google.api.http binding (Transcoded).\n\nLeast privilege by default: an undeclared method is not_found; Serve refuses\na module absent from api.consumes, a method without a binding under\n/v1/<as>, a streaming method, and a method that names no response fields;\nresponses carry only the fields the declaration names unless WholeResponse\nis explicit. A module''s refusal reaches the page in the Connect error.\nPassthroughOperations documents the declaration for the interface artifact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"b7a0a4cb4bea11bbc02b8c027c756f4d72a8ecb2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/b7a0a4cb4bea11bbc02b8c027c756f4d72a8ecb2"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/001880b1541f410f7b4a622e1383d720b960d001","verification":{"payload":"tree b7a0a4cb4bea11bbc02b8c027c756f4d72a8ecb2\nparent 2007f853dcfbc2fca718ee1539f37d39093165db\nauthor Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790350297 -0400\ncommitter Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790350297 -0400\n\nfeat: let a solution''s page call a consumed module''s declared operations\n\nA page reaches only its solution''s own backend, so every module read it made\nneeded a handler in the solution that decoded the request, minted the\nviewer''s capability, called the module and re-encoded the answer: the same\nrelay in every solution, once per operation.\n\nServer.Consumes declares instead which operations of which consumed module\nthe page may call. Each is served as a Connect unary procedure at\n/modules/<as>/<package.Service>/<Method>, so the module''s generated client is\nused unmodified. A call is answered by the module as the viewer: the runtime\nmints the declared Work Context (ForModule), or forwards only the bearer to a\nmodule that authenticates the viewer itself, and forwards the request over\nthe method''s google.api.http binding (Transcoded).\n\nLeast privilege by default: an undeclared method is not_found; Serve refuses\na module absent from api.consumes, a method without a binding under\n/v1/<as>, a streaming method, and a method that names no response fields;\nresponses carry only the fields the declaration names unless WholeResponse\nis explicit. A module''s refusal reaches the page in the Connect error.\nPassthroughOperations documents the declaration for the interface artifact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcdDfnJkwhq+GcBoTN3TX56bX0H\n8InRU9/eZzzo1eEkwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQO67GGh5WCLudTf1b31a3cEYSwKD8TXpLObHf4L/WFPnz+tU/g/OFUqLWM99aAvNy4\ncjAoYtvTvWC/HuDjBw9gE=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T15:35:52Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","foll