nA handler that must check a claimed owner against the capability it reads\nwith had to mint its own Task Work Context (with an invented session) to see\naccounts'' owner and actor. Gateway.WorkContextPrincipals returns the\norganization, owner and current actor accounts answered the ForModule mint\nwith, reusing the cached capability.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"e40ce95515a720f1364e953d7549374597faf7be","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/e40ce95515a720f1364e953d7549374597faf7be"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/d5e5c50e17123da9d89822764a991bd4ee546456","verification":{"payload":"tree e40ce95515a720f1364e953d7549374597faf7be\nparent 9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988\nauthor Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790326314 -0400\ncommitter Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790326314 -0400\n\nfeat: report whom a ForModule capability was issued for\n\nA handler that must check a claimed owner against the capability it reads\nwith had to mint its own Task Work Context (with an invented session) to see\naccounts'' owner and actor. Gateway.WorkContextPrincipals returns the\norganization, owner and current actor accounts answered the ForModule mint\nwith, reusing the cached capability.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcdDfnJkwhq+GcBoTN3TX56bX0H\n8InRU9/eZzzo1eEkwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQIgpqCx1bK9SJSF7t9qWaZYlD/21BJmu6br5X5MbkxzCG+l9TVS3813ACkihEsBlm9\nsxCymfxWGo48bRV4mjwA4=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T08:51:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/d5e5c50e17123da9d89822764a991bd4ee546456","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKGQ1ZTVjNTBlMTcxMjNkYTlkODk4MjI3NjRhOTkxYmQ0ZWU1NDY0NTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988","sha":"9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988"}],"sha":"d5e5c50e17123da9d89822764a991bd4ee546456","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/d5e5c50e17123da9d89822764a991bd4ee546456"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-25T08:40:52Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-25T08:40:52Z","email":"312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com","name":"Antoine Toussaint"},"message":"feat: call composed modules over their REST binding; documented operations\n\nA solution reaches a composed module only under the REST prefix it federates\n(/v1/<as>/*), so the module''s generated gRPC/Connect client cannot be pointed\nat the gateway, and solutions were hand-building paths, query strings and wire\nstructs for every module read. Gateway.Transcoded calls an RPC with the\nmodule''s own generated messages over the method''s google.api.http binding\nunder the consumed prefix. Everything about the request comes from the\ndescriptor: the caller names no path, and a method with no binding under the\nprefix is refused before anything is sent.\n\nAlongside it, what a handler needs to hand an owner''s message on:\nMessage[T] encodes a generated message as protobuf JSON inside a response,\nand FieldMask/Apply pass on only a declared allowlist of its fields, so an\nowner field added later reaches no browser until someone names it.\n\nOperation, Server.Operations and InterfaceDocument move the documented-route\ndeclaration and its Swagger 2.0 artifact into the runtime, so one list is the\nsource of what a solution serves and what it publishes. A Message[T] field is\ndescribed from its descriptor.\n\nGateway.OrgID exposes the active organization ForModule mints in, so a handler\nscopes a module read to the same tenant its capability names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ee24dce47200a895671cae1a6de9f960fd3f3118","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/ee24dce47200a895671cae1a6de9f960fd3f3118"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988","verification":{"payload":"tree ee24dce47200a895671cae1a6de9f960fd3f3118\nparent 89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19\nauthor Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790325652 -0400\ncommitter Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com> 1790325652 -0400\n\nfeat: call composed modules over their REST binding; documented operations\n\nA solution reaches a composed module only under the REST prefix it federates\n(/v1/<as>/*), so the module''s generated gRPC/Connect client cannot be pointed\nat the gateway, and solutions were hand-building paths, query strings and wire\nstructs for every module read. Gateway.Transcoded calls an RPC with the\nmodule''s own generated messages over the method''s google.api.http binding\nunder the consumed prefix. Everything about the request comes from the\ndescriptor: the caller names no path, and a method with no binding under the\nprefix is refused before anything is sent.\n\nAlongside it, what a handler needs to hand an owner''s message on:\nMessage[T] encodes a generated message as protobuf JSON inside a response,\nand FieldMask/Apply pass on only a declared allowlist of its fields, so an\nowner field added later reaches no browser until someone names it.\n\nOperation, Server.Operations and InterfaceDocument move the documented-route\ndeclaration and its Swagger 2.0 artifact into the runtime, so one list is the\nsource of what a solution serves and what it publishes. A Message[T] field is\ndescribed from its descriptor.\n\nGateway.OrgID exposes the active organization ForModule mints in, so a handler\nscopes a module read to the same tenant its capability names.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN SSH SIGNATURE-----\nU1NIU0lHAAAAAQAAADMAAAALc3NoLWVkMjU1MTkAAAAgcdDfnJkwhq+GcBoTN3TX56bX0H\n8InRU9/eZzzo1eEkwAAAADZ2l0AAAAAAAAAAZzaGE1MTIAAABTAAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5\nAAAAQBLFSy5vP0ZOZIZnAK2TeGtwmLlwOWTla91umzDBY0fVEMN+693LuXg4vgwqYonX20\nsuyG2NaJFbYcJ/03rXXgM=\n-----END SSH SIGNATURE-----","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-25T08:40:54Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDliN2M0YzU5NDFiOGViNmM1YjExMmUwZjYxMmQwOTk0M2NhOTU5ODg","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19","sha":"89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19"}],"sha":"9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/9b7c4c5941b8eb6c5b112e0f612d09943ca95988"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-24T00:16:56Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-24T00:16:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix!: register addresses a deployed solution can actually be reached at (#37)\n\nA deployed solution registered `manifestUrl: http://localhost:8080/assets/mf-manifest.json`\nand upstream `http://localhost:8080` — its own listen address, via the\nPUBLIC_URL default — so the product showed \"solution failed to load\" and the\ngateway proxied the solution to itself. Both booted and looked healthy.\n\n- manifestUrl: with no PUBLIC_URL, register the root-relative path\n  /assets/mf-manifest.json on the solution''s own backend; the host resolves it\n  against the route by which it reaches the solution. The runtime does not\n  encode the host''s route layout. BREAKING on the wire: the host must resolve a\n  root-relative manifestUrl (the parallel module-saas-starter change).\n- upstream: take it from the reachable self endpoint Codefly injects as\n  CODEFLY__SELF_ENDPOINT__<MODULE>__<SERVICE>__HTTP__HTTP (core v0.5.6), falling\n  back to the listen address; SELF_UPSTREAM still overrides, PUBLIC_URL no\n  longer feeds it. Labelled stopgap: the carrier is read by name in one helper\n  until core/sdk-go release an accessor.\n- validate(): refuse a loopback upstream or PUBLIC_URL when\n  CODEFLY__RUNTIME_CONTEXT names a deployed runtime (anything outside\n  native/nix/container/free, e.g. a GitOps render''s \"kubernetes\", core v0.5.6).\n  Never keyed on the environment name.\n- exchange: only 401/403 name the SOLUTION_REGISTRATION_SECRETS provisioning; a\n  5xx reports \"host unavailable (status N), retrying\" with the gateway''s body,\n  other statuses a failure with their body; the heartbeat keeps retrying.\n- Manifest.Assets fs.FS: when set, /assets/ is served from it (nothing read\n  from disk, so a read-only root filesystem works); else ASSETS_DIR as before.\n  Content-hashed files are cached immutable, everything else and every\n  non-file response no-cache.\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"6f6fac709b715c14a9289e93bb8a57596a70c5e1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/6f6fac709b715c14a9289e93bb8a57596a70c5e1"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19","verification":{"payload":"tree 6f6fac709b715c14a9289e93bb8a57596a70c5e1\nparent d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1790209016 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790209016 -0400\n\nfix!: register addresses a deployed solution can actually be reached at (#37)\n\nA deployed solution registered `manifestUrl: http://localhost:8080/assets/mf-manifest.json`\nand upstream `http://localhost:8080` — its own listen address, via the\nPUBLIC_URL default — so the product showed \"solution failed to load\" and the\ngateway proxied the solution to itself. Both booted and looked healthy.\n\n- manifestUrl: with no PUBLIC_URL, register the root-relative path\n  /assets/mf-manifest.json on the solution''s own backend; the host resolves it\n  against the route by which it reaches the solution. The runtime does not\n  encode the host''s route layout. BREAKING on the wire: the host must resolve a\n  root-relative manifestUrl (the parallel module-saas-starter change).\n- upstream: take it from the reachable self endpoint Codefly injects as\n  CODEFLY__SELF_ENDPOINT__<MODULE>__<SERVICE>__HTTP__HTTP (core v0.5.6), falling\n  back to the listen address; SELF_UPSTREAM still overrides, PUBLIC_URL no\n  longer feeds it. Labelled stopgap: the carrier is read by name in one helper\n  until core/sdk-go release an accessor.\n- validate(): refuse a loopback upstream or PUBLIC_URL when\n  CODEFLY__RUNTIME_CONTEXT names a deployed runtime (anything outside\n  native/nix/container/free, e.g. a GitOps render''s \"kubernetes\", core v0.5.6).\n  Never keyed on the environment name.\n- exchange: only 401/403 name the SOLUTION_REGISTRATION_SECRETS provisioning; a\n  5xx reports \"host unavailable (status N), retrying\" with the gateway''s body,\n  other statuses a failure with their body; the heartbeat keeps retrying.\n- Manifest.Assets fs.FS: when set, /assets/ is served from it (nothing read\n  from disk, so a read-only root filesystem works); else ASSETS_DIR as before.\n  Content-hashed files are cached immutable, everything else and every\n  non-file response no-cache.\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtGv4CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAhe8QAIy6hQCIy2RSWfsDHaOBgYT2\nOtxbP0jn/hcWaa2+jon5dRTkwdiSQsnNDlD6fpwLaHvoPbgHvJNiksln7qUulXQn\nTTGLXEYfHAJbMkPYS+QQeLIbhpIdz9FotRrG9Ndyy994UbXkeMRAomPgP5VMFynI\nJHWy9/WfseesMKIpabXFlD36bnIGb8EU3J5Lpy3QJP1IAE8ImxCb2raeJCB/kS1v\nj++hjni6nnOMOmw/Su2C3sTK6FP2/7hIM/78i/G755un5JUUu9gVqDJ4jDHjAxDs\nd3oATMYJ/mKC6EsZq/VAH2RTwU5PC3FedUXP0GiY1pSdmFCU28b8hG3GqQz/gt0Y\nU+k3H6hye1d73rA0Sy9FRacu4yZ2JvmnOEGyJxCKLhCbEmw+3gPfwQhuAPeGAFwO\nWRYWaPx6YRv3tp1wctJydvfcfd3Q63i9fC8T8DVQ3QmLk5G7Yq2vA15IpsVOPvjq\n4LHYOyah6sY2djnGPP2Sr9gMnRRkk1Rbe26qWWEsAHf/ldcW7V50CpxfwaQfxUO1\nYJNac9mUkNt1JG7Eu3s1txYF2qwGd1qb2uSSkPneCbJA+zg0cV1fsKKjYOPUnGTS\nDHAOE3vYymh4L7AWq32SpQGNJdk7r1UvYFuNh/P03qsrBz3U19yAdajNeyIrKa1p\nMa13kQb8D7s35z33ZaTt\n=8xUU\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-24T00:16:56Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDg5ZTFhZWFiMTJiZTI2NWI4YmY1ZTU5MGQzY2UzMjU1ZTE1NzRmMTk","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a","sha":"d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a"}],"sha":"89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/89e1aeab12be265b8bf5e590d3ce3255e1574f19"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-23T19:39:40Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-23T19:39:40Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: read the listen port from a bare host:port self endpoint (#36)\n\nCodefly hands a service its own endpoint as a bare host:port (a rendered cell\nwrites \"localhost:8080\"); url.Parse reads that as scheme \"localhost\" with no\nport, so every rendered solution refused to boot with ''unresolved listen port\n\"\"''. listenPort accepts both the bare form and a URL.\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c3892402f5708b847c9373ec58f82f108d9993b9","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/c3892402f5708b847c9373ec58f82f108d9993b9"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a","verification":{"payload":"tree c3892402f5708b847c9373ec58f82f108d9993b9\nparent 0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1790192380 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790192380 -0400\n\nfix: read the listen port from a bare host:port self endpoint (#36)\n\nCodefly hands a service its own endpoint as a bare host:port (a rendered cell\nwrites \"localhost:8080\"); url.Parse reads that as scheme \"localhost\" with no\nport, so every rendered solution refused to boot with ''unresolved listen port\n\"\"''. listenPort accepts both the bare form and a URL.\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqtCr8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAq0gQAGNGGnd6Wv7x3YwVXhjn0vAY\nM4Vf+zy1+HhPNg+6NE4HH6kMZtDo2B6onKhu+h5WVLrzRogSptn9sVata76gamDd\nal28CCrqZvDgps1RnS5HGVlAB56vOrFYSSDFHm1f2nDK4uYKSi2ACe8OHBJsEyHR\n5L9hEC/bHh3uz2w2yn8XY6wVUN42lpuQYRwsxuGGs7eVamGDn+SPls6Dn1eQUtmY\nkwhQh4UCirV/74se/FUIFnKWXit9vTYwvoN5AMeFkHQH8cxxh7nuxt5VhfuTX0eo\n7jo3yrUl/icRvKtkwiXhhOjdXvTNViYOcbU+3ONXI3LjmDmdZJC6RsJsaLZeQoHv\ng1tLovdqR4bhvf7qurC4xrttx1SiOhH7pPszmSjbzyIELKvP1bkjjlDfBZlZPxrv\nxLvlOmVAEzSHdr1E/Qe1VHdMRuvbVOrTNnOGok724v/XbpYKJPrzN/uz0hueDAAr\nKXuD48mxGLY/yhrAU5CdwMbtuhu+l+shqKz6CcXRBgjfyTBNPMqh+KnkRRaJRiod\nbkR/YCiV0tC+vLAzIHjIvxClRFTyHEuIjz1eanmVulX7+VXVvgLUCoqgM6PK0KPK\nwFpVoybqkDx+6sP/peNUYCN/OxLb3mzQw/K1BpozX59vKk3In+kba8a5RQ99v31K\nXALh3HZtbY2tO6/yIB80\n=H2Ff\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-23T19:39:40Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKGQzMTQwM2UxMDlhMzM3Y2ExNGRjZjE3N2ExN2UwOWQwNTg4NGEzN2E","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c","sha":"0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c"}],"sha":"d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/d31403e109a337ca14dcf177a17e09d05884a37a"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:58:49Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:58:49Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"docs: state the agent contract for this repo (#30) (#35)\n\n* docs: state the agent contract for this repo (#30)\n\nAn agent starting here had no statement of what this runtime owns, what it\ndoes not, or how to behave when something does not work. The failure that\nproduced the fleet standard was measured against these runtimes: an agent\nhand-wrote the environment they exist to resolve, and a sibling runtime\nskipped registration silently.\n\nCommands are derived from the workflow and were run in this worktree.\n\nRefs obin-ai/handbook#68\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct two claims the code does not support (#30)\n\nReview of the new file found it asserting a safety property this runtime\ndoes not have: the consumed-API projection is read at serve time, never\nreaches validate(), and a malformed one degrades to a log line while the\nsolution serves. A file stating otherwise would send an agent toward the\nsilent absence the rules exist to prevent, so the exception is now stated\nas the dangerous path it is.\n\nThe exported surface was also enumerated partially, omitting Manifest,\nHandler, RequestHandler and the exported constants — read as exhaustive,\nit would let a breaking change ship without a bang.\n\nAlso drops an invented rationale for CI''s test timeout and records the\nstale v0.0.2 Release object rather than implying tags are the only artifact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: pin the configuration boundary AGENTS.md states (#30)\n\nThe file now tells an agent that boot configuration is resolved in\nloadConfig and refused by validate(), with one serve-time exception whose\nfailure is a log line rather than a refusal. That claim was prose with\nnothing holding it: a second interior read would make the file quietly\nwrong again, which is the defect the file was just corrected for.\n\nThe guard is structural rather than a list of function names — an\nenumeration rots the same way the exported-surface list did. It asserts\nevery environment read sits in loadConfig''s call tree, where validate()\ngoverns the result, or is the documented exception; that the exception\nstill reads the environment and is still unreachable from loadConfig; and\nthat this file still names it.\n\nProven red three ways before landing: an os.Getenv added to a serve-path\nhandler, the exception''s name removed from AGENTS.md, and the exception''s\nown read replaced by a constant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c17c3d74c510d085ddf0932435f6acefcf535108","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/c17c3d74c510d085ddf0932435f6acefcf535108"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c","verification":{"payload":"tree c17c3d74c510d085ddf0932435f6acefcf535108\nparent 2ce3204d3f87d34294b87c2eea54818e05222a9f\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1790103529 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790103529 -0400\n\ndocs: state the agent contract for this repo (#30) (#35)\n\n* docs: state the agent contract for this repo (#30)\n\nAn agent starting here had no statement of what this runtime owns, what it\ndoes not, or how to behave when something does not work. The failure that\nproduced the fleet standard was measured against these runtimes: an agent\nhand-wrote the environment they exist to resolve, and a sibling runtime\nskipped registration silently.\n\nCommands are derived from the workflow and were run in this worktree.\n\nRefs obin-ai/handbook#68\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* docs: correct two claims the code does not support (#30)\n\nReview of the new file found it asserting a safety property this runtime\ndoes not have: the consumed-API projection is read at serve time, never\nreaches validate(), and a malformed one degrades to a log line while the\nsolution serves. A file stating otherwise would send an agent toward the\nsilent absence the rules exist to prevent, so the exception is now stated\nas the dangerous path it is.\n\nThe exported surface was also enumerated partially, omitting Manifest,\nHandler, RequestHandler and the exported constants — read as exhaustive,\nit would let a breaking change ship without a bang.\n\nAlso drops an invented rationale for CI''s test timeout and records the\nstale v0.0.2 Release object rather than implying tags are the only artifact.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* test: pin the configuration boundary AGENTS.md states (#30)\n\nThe file now tells an agent that boot configuration is resolved in\nloadConfig and refused by validate(), with one serve-time exception whose\nfailure is a log line rather than a refusal. That claim was prose with\nnothing holding it: a second interior read would make the file quietly\nwrong again, which is the defect the file was just corrected for.\n\nThe guard is structural rather than a list of function names — an\nenumeration rots the same way the exported-surface list did. It asserts\nevery environment read sits in loadConfig''s call tree, where validate()\ngoverns the result, or is the documented exception; that the exception\nstill reads the environment and is still unreachable from loadConfig; and\nthat this file still names it.\n\nProven red three ways before landing: an os.Getenv added to a serve-path\nhandler, the exception''s name removed from AGENTS.md, and the exception''s\nown read replaced by a constant.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqss/pCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAACfwQAKwj45KIOWms2yRuuv7lq+Ki\nxT//ewojzYOvV0mseVnVnnjljIc/oWmGmwthzs+Om9810oU5JDngg0S14wquiHLt\n4QoHFZqn7qpMERRashHBdP8OSZVD5WNYXGS8bojsWm14oJ3yeAHCcsJwp9lG/y1V\nQTK0yAl8BXMIILIH6DfJ5was+GIVKlrjrdg8+2S48RtAUD6XR2XditwNL1YYU5hP\nPu6EazuB+RmpRfZgafo/55B39yVpY9SR1dv+X4utfOm3Cvm71fyLbVf/SGFsRbtJ\nxviG+yl8Fo4vdc1j0ATAuTMN4JHleE1zkt1epbjsRtapuGaSzuT+jvpM4ixviazj\nwh+i72YVfjTAmow3QT2Ifyf8CYTX9FHSnWl3RhSwE5LHCfPeIJ/vIDveKN/l8TGW\n607wgX9umRAzEm5CuJi+YkSXWXY6zyTU0Za+8oeSzgyAVrWmCBDvTs6lFLvHNdiM\nz76TPVdVc8xL7CwZtU2LCIhPsDfmM3yx7Lq+qgaI+SUgVLsfsivIRh3dpcP9cxpW\nOTQINe6iJX9t0E1T88YX7U0OuNA8E+i1tKLebXQJBM5JqDMlq/eqgALwc+33hCdi\nqWk5WX0RDdSiTkBLwCp8vHKNXMMxDdWc+Jl+lTWcbEhYbBFD2MkAJrG6Uf0T7RqR\n6EoLr/Ak69arBFWxf4qN\n=0kIY\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T18:58:50Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDBhOTk3Y2FkOGIzYWI0MDhhZjA3ZDQ4ZWVjZWY5M2QwOTY3MjU0OGM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/2ce3204d3f87d34294b87c2eea54818e05222a9f","sha":"2ce3204d3f87d34294b87c2eea54818e05222a9f","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/2ce3204d3f87d34294b87c2eea54818e05222a9f"}],"sha":"0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/0a997cad8b3ab408af07d48eecef93d09672548c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/2ce3204d3f87d34294b87c2eea54818e05222a9f/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:58:41Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-22T18:58:41Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: declare client surfaces in the solution manifest (#32) (#34)\n\n* feat: declare client surfaces in the solution manifest\n\nA solution can offer something inside a client — the wiki offers citing\ninside a Word document — and until now the add-in carried a table of who\noffers what. Manifest gains Surfaces, served beside nav and dashboard, so\na client discovers the offering from the solution''s own declaration.\n\nThe runtime validates what a client cannot recover from: a well-formed,\nunique id, a known client kind, and a module path on the solution''s own\norigin. applies and events are carried verbatim, like dashboard — what a\ntag selects and what a namespace names are the client''s to interpret.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: close the surface validations that let an unusable surface through\n\nThe module check did not hold. A browser resolves \"/\\host/x.js\" by\nreading the backslash as a slash and what follows as an authority, so it\nloads https://host/x.js, while net/url reads that backslash as an\nordinary path byte and reports no host — the check asked net/url and so\naccepted it. ASCII tab and newline are removed by that same parser before\nit parses, turning \"/<tab>/host/x.js\" protocol-relative on arrival; those\nwere refused only because net/url happens to reject control characters.\nBoth are now refused by inspecting the bytes, because what makes a path\nrooted is the parser that will resolve it, not the one validating it.\nThe check catches an author''s mistake, which is all a validation here can\ndo: a solution serves its own manifest, so the host''s registry and the\nclient''s loader still own that boundary.\n\nA zero Contract was emitted as \"contract\": 0. A client runs a surface\nonly when it recognises the major it declares, so that shipped a surface\nevery client refuses, from a boot that looked healthy and logged nothing\n— the silent no-op the rest of this runtime''s validation exists to\nprevent. An empty Title had the same shape one step further out: a\nclient labels the surface with it and renders a blank control. Both are\nnow refused at boot.\n\nSurface ids were unique per solution, which refused the ordinary case of\none offering in two clients — \"footnote\" in Word and in PowerPoint. Two\nclients never see each other''s surfaces, so only a collision within one\nclient is ambiguous; the key is now (client, id).\n\nAn undeclared Applies was omitted, leaving every client to invent the\nsame default for a surface that is otherwise fully declared. It is now\nserved as \"always\". Description and Events keep being omitted when\nempty: absent, those say something a client can act on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"c5947aa68e14bdfd3a1381f7df2b5e2714c82c28","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/c5947aa68e14bdfd3a1381f7df2b5e2714c82c28"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/2ce3204d3f87d34294b87c2eea54818e05222a9f","verification":{"payload":"tree c5947aa68e14bdfd3a1381f7df2b5e2714c82c28\nparent 24f6e4b0a163ebb6bbab545754c4a0b7e25cf735\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1790103521 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1790103521 -0400\n\nfeat: declare client surfaces in the solution manifest (#32) (#34)\n\n* feat: declare client surfaces in the solution manifest\n\nA solution can offer something inside a client — the wiki offers citing\ninside a Word document — and until now the add-in carried a table of who\noffers what. Manifest gains Surfaces, served beside nav and dashboard, so\na client discovers the offering from the solution''s own declaration.\n\nThe runtime validates what a client cannot recover from: a well-formed,\nunique id, a known client kind, and a module path on the solution''s own\norigin. applies and events are carried verbatim, like dashboard — what a\ntag selects and what a namespace names are the client''s to interpret.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: close the surface validations that let an unusable surface through\n\nThe module check did not hold. A browser resolves \"/\\host/x.js\" by\nreading the backslash as a slash and what follows as an authority, so it\nloads https://host/x.js, while net/url reads that backslash as an\nordinary path byte and reports no host — the check asked net/url and so\naccepted it. ASCII tab and newline are removed by that same parser before\nit parses, turning \"/<tab>/host/x.js\" protocol-relative on arrival; those\nwere refused only because net/url happens to reject control characters.\nBoth are now refused by inspecting the bytes, because what makes a path\nrooted is the parser that will resolve it, not the one validating it.\nThe check catches an author''s mistake, which is all a validation here can\ndo: a solution serves its own manifest, so the host''s registry and the\nclient''s loader still own that boundary.\n\nA zero Contract was emitted as \"contract\": 0. A client runs a surface\nonly when it recognises the major it declares, so that shipped a surface\nevery client refuses, from a boot that looked healthy and logged nothing\n— the silent no-op the rest of this runtime''s validation exists to\nprevent. An empty Title had the same shape one step further out: a\nclient labels the surface with it and renders a blank control. Both are\nnow refused at boot.\n\nSurface ids were unique per solution, which refused the ordinary case of\none offering in two clients — \"footnote\" in Word and in PowerPoint. Two\nclients never see each other''s surfaces, so only a collision within one\nclient is ambiguous; the key is now (client, id).\n\nAn undeclared Applies was omitted, leaving every client to invent the\nsame default for a surface that is otherwise fully declared. It is now\nserved as \"always\". Description and Events keep being omitted when\nempty: absent, those say something a client can act on.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Antoine Toussaint <312536060+antoinetoussaint-byte@users.noreply.github.com>\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqss/hCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAMmwQAHgvnANQpyG2OpyjaXbhvBUj\ndnt1fRDtiueRwcYVbXvJytE89O2MvTzXM7Xb+zJgFJkCSbiOrDGq/saZfOL90bbv\nnSIQD+MUqKev3PBLvni8ENQYH2a8DleAImzWN5+A4rreQjldk1eef1QOQTvqy9+s\nAiP+mUOU+9XgSaLdVeE71Gyj1cmdIKacuZ2NVcZ09HyJde3d4CeWhbPVWt15/Q3f\nRw3hK1pXJizAMSgCRUjNh2RYEtkUMisE9P9u+sVHg64Ykp0nGb8afAEkT3zSuprc\nLQcZCDOpBs/T3RcXa6kxbHeGco1BJyAfN91TAshu0kg2s3428xB8PjlxCEMO/6V3\nq19c2g6kk3Y2gHiFKV1AXKgAMJ3ECqSvwB/GuVf1XG41InfkRFHssDcGdvhdpU9G\nvIswiw7bpPlZc5Z2wkP1ctQxVWoA3FJwd/JpYcfUB9DyWUCkfP+K6yFIw4J4LNfm\nYt6MaunPpEUA0GoIUddAvVRW2GSjkcLMhTmLvR9uDfvftxWeca42iTtVabRuYc+O\neFA0vP1+vBFM4vJrFSNNIpLw2h6hpPmjaObKCB0wCrpm79VTqC1sJmRkEQ2r+RvQ\n5IuyPP30jSQLHRVHWg2mVDPQ03wMy/2e7IKIJZu2g7kNHHJc8fcHwX3+VTpMrkxq\nxMTCi2WzCIQ7GLPeVyse\n=OPfo\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-22T18:58:42Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avat