inetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/451cea7e8202c3aa68f54ff1e0a8975fcad2d7bc","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDQ1MWNlYTdlODIwMmMzYWE2OGY1NGZmMWUwYTg5NzVmY2FkMmQ3YmM","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/487bc20d6c6d11808ce86f3aa78dc7af895bff42","sha":"487bc20d6c6d11808ce86f3aa78dc7af895bff42","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/487bc20d6c6d11808ce86f3aa78dc7af895bff42"}],"sha":"451cea7e8202c3aa68f54ff1e0a8975fcad2d7bc","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/451cea7e8202c3aa68f54ff1e0a8975fcad2d7bc"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/487bc20d6c6d11808ce86f3aa78dc7af895bff42/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:32:12Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-14T16:32:12Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: root module-read Work Contexts in the viewer''s verified session (#28) (#29)\n\n* feat: root module-read Work Contexts in the viewer''s verified session (#28)\n\nA solution reading a composed module minted a Task Work Context whose\nsession id was a fresh UUID. It passed accounts'' validation — the field\nis only constrained to be a UUID — while naming no session at all, so\nnothing about the viewer''s session reached the capability minted under\nit: an organization switch, an ended impersonation, a revoked or expired\nsession left it just as valid.\n\nThe session now comes from x-session-id, stamped by the gateway from the\nsame verified claims as x-org-id and replacing anything the caller sent.\nThat is the session accounts sealed the selected organization into, so\nthe capability follows the org the viewer actually switched into and\nlapses with the session. Only the Task id is minted per ask.\n\nA caller with no session to name — an API key authenticates a principal\nand no session — is refused at the boundary, like a caller with no\nactive org, rather than charged an audited mint accounts would refuse.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: answer module-read refusals with an actionable status, and stop claiming revocation (#28)\n\nForModule refuses a caller it cannot name both boundaries for, but returned a\nbare error — which wrapRequest maps to 502. A viewer who merely has no\norganization selected, something they fix in one click, got an outage-shaped\nresponse the frontend cannot tell apart from a dead solution, and the refusal''s\ndiagnostic (naming internal headers) became the public response body.\n\nBoth refusals now carry a ClientError, the mechanism this file already documents\nfor a 4xx: 409 for no organization selected, 403 for no session. The header\ndiagnostic is wrapped behind %w, so it stays in the handler''s error and out of\nthe caller''s response — the separation ClientError exists to provide.\n\nThe 403 is the deliberate answer for a caller that authenticates without a\nsession, i.e. an API key, and the README now says outright that such a caller\ncannot read a composed module. Accounts requires a Task to name a session\n(session_id is a required UUID on StartTask), and the only id this runtime could\nsupply is an invented one — which is precisely what made the capability\nattributable to nothing. The user-absent path accounts does provide is the\nheadless installation mint, which this runtime does not implement.\n\nThe session-binding comments and README also claimed the capability \"lapses with\nthe session\" and that a revocation reaches it. It does not: the edge verifies a\npresented context''s signature and validity window, not the liveness of the\nsession named in it, so revoking a session stops the next request while an\nalready-minted capability stands until its own expiry. That claim is replaced\nwith what the binding actually buys — attribution — and an explicit note that\nrevocation is not part of it, because a security property documented but not\nimplemented is worse than one never claimed.\n\nFinally, the cache was documented as keyed \"per (org, session, audience,\nscopes)\". It lives for one request, so org and session are fixed across it and\ncannot tell two asks apart; reworded to the ask itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"60e14f48e520dd769e6d60f0b75f10a74d92b791","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/60e14f48e520dd769e6d60f0b75f10a74d92b791"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/487bc20d6c6d11808ce86f3aa78dc7af895bff42","verification":{"payload":"tree 60e14f48e520dd769e6d60f0b75f10a74d92b791\nparent 0e14e5182230eb6e893a50e3367b11059d7f26f4\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1789403532 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789403532 -0400\n\nfeat: root module-read Work Contexts in the viewer''s verified session (#28) (#29)\n\n* feat: root module-read Work Contexts in the viewer''s verified session (#28)\n\nA solution reading a composed module minted a Task Work Context whose\nsession id was a fresh UUID. It passed accounts'' validation — the field\nis only constrained to be a UUID — while naming no session at all, so\nnothing about the viewer''s session reached the capability minted under\nit: an organization switch, an ended impersonation, a revoked or expired\nsession left it just as valid.\n\nThe session now comes from x-session-id, stamped by the gateway from the\nsame verified claims as x-org-id and replacing anything the caller sent.\nThat is the session accounts sealed the selected organization into, so\nthe capability follows the org the viewer actually switched into and\nlapses with the session. Only the Task id is minted per ask.\n\nA caller with no session to name — an API key authenticates a principal\nand no session — is refused at the boundary, like a caller with no\nactive org, rather than charged an audited mint accounts would refuse.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: answer module-read refusals with an actionable status, and stop claiming revocation (#28)\n\nForModule refuses a caller it cannot name both boundaries for, but returned a\nbare error — which wrapRequest maps to 502. A viewer who merely has no\norganization selected, something they fix in one click, got an outage-shaped\nresponse the frontend cannot tell apart from a dead solution, and the refusal''s\ndiagnostic (naming internal headers) became the public response body.\n\nBoth refusals now carry a ClientError, the mechanism this file already documents\nfor a 4xx: 409 for no organization selected, 403 for no session. The header\ndiagnostic is wrapped behind %w, so it stays in the handler''s error and out of\nthe caller''s response — the separation ClientError exists to provide.\n\nThe 403 is the deliberate answer for a caller that authenticates without a\nsession, i.e. an API key, and the README now says outright that such a caller\ncannot read a composed module. Accounts requires a Task to name a session\n(session_id is a required UUID on StartTask), and the only id this runtime could\nsupply is an invented one — which is precisely what made the capability\nattributable to nothing. The user-absent path accounts does provide is the\nheadless installation mint, which this runtime does not implement.\n\nThe session-binding comments and README also claimed the capability \"lapses with\nthe session\" and that a revocation reaches it. It does not: the edge verifies a\npresented context''s signature and validity window, not the liveness of the\nsession named in it, so revoking a session stops the next request while an\nalready-minted capability stands until its own expiry. That claim is replaced\nwith what the binding actually buys — attribution — and an explicit note that\nrevocation is not part of it, because a security property documented but not\nimplemented is worse than one never claimed.\n\nFinally, the cache was documented as keyed \"per (org, session, audience,\nscopes)\". It lives for one request, so org and session are fixed across it and\ncannot tell two asks apart; reworded to the ask itself.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqqCGMCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJ1sQAC9h11/b8VpbKl3jAEWYSvTf\n+sf5PysuGLl46rpRssCCSkCkw7m0QwRdyuBLwrEkG0Pr7aSLD5yNnZuxndE