equest handlers owned input validation but could only report failures as 502. Add a typed ClientError carried through the shared response wrapper so handlers can explicitly return 4xx responses, including wrapped validation errors, while preserving ordinary upstream error behavior. Cover malformed and oversized bodies, semantic validation, invalid statuses, and legacy handlers.","tree":{"sha":"502f808f659931afaf02496ae2fd64e541c2a1bb","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/502f808f659931afaf02496ae2fd64e541c2a1bb"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/0e14e5182230eb6e893a50e3367b11059d7f26f4","verification":{"payload":"tree 502f808f659931afaf02496ae2fd64e541c2a1bb\nparent e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1789162587 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789162587 -0400\n\nAllow authenticated solution handlers to consume request input (#27)\n\n* feat: let authenticated solution handlers consume request input\n\n* fix: let handlers report request validation failures as client errors\n\nRequest handlers owned input validation but could only report failures as 502. Add a typed ClientError carried through the shared response wrapper so handlers can explicitly return 4xx responses, including wrapped validation errors, while preserving ordinary upstream error behavior. Cover malformed and oversized bodies, semantic validation, invalid statuses, and legacy handlers.","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqpHRbCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAUjUQAJIIDodusCkgPoUYGTAqJtSP\nuOyPJuaImnWG4MN6n/4aFy2oLO2vTrlVeC0RblIUK+8Le8pvFtQ8lJAf72pHMW7o\nw/1kSdZwgGHMS/Y/ORBEq9eHbigbGaYkjYxO5VuHpyMyObWjIqpOr90gp2eiv2oH\nog0jvkQjv8HU0a8GEGkLFjFLc1XuLlycUKS7uC9RUDX7bssjMQMQRDBrbY5HIuS8\n6XRViUnVQHsVxHkqvK5ECssvmPirZbK7AzDWwQl4aoQHgtNtljJYM1V0wtTmP9zm\ndtysOgv+JhUaQCOOqOF5GhWKChGCTaikQPvrhZgydWXXIxGaoIE6I+KlFmLjroZp\nQtZsZqL/O/NcTvJ1qRjKDrWsdcdxCGsbYv3W6z8QBu6gKJbksIiTTToIHgaRP7v+\n4H2/xv2DACtM3ILo9fxb1XBnUHA+LeEVhz1eQWymQZeJUaOWn6OnUbGZIXRokhuU\nzqEf9VfF1t3f7y/cB0PmUtI2emG9HQtKvCdiRJGLjI8Zb8gtCj9Ekrfl3Ad2G2NZ\nj0z2MSfBGxk6IEcRQMop8mbO/dXdvpWLa1arAtObrAGD7nssCsPp1PiVZc6avQhG\nv7xl3pxCrLPupSWBPdvih0TvqROwSa/xEYyYoJGqOUp5KFvtndNkQwm4ZL50nL8y\nCg0pRnYobn2XInU4ReZ4\n=RQq3\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T21:36:28Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/0e14e5182230eb6e893a50e3367b11059d7f26f4","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDBlMTRlNTE4MjIzMGViNmU4OTNhNTBlMzM2N2IxMTA1OWQ3ZjI2ZjQ","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6","sha":"e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6"}],"sha":"0e14e5182230eb6e893a50e3367b11059d7f26f4","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/0e14e5182230eb6e893a50e3367b11059d7f26f4"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:05:56Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T12:05:56Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat!: fail closed on solution registration — no cluster-internal-token fallback (#26)\n\n* feat!: fail closed on solution registration — no cluster-internal-token fallback\n\nThe shared cluster-internal token proves no publisher, so it is never\npresented on a registration. A boot without a provisioned secret is refused\nby validate(), naming the provisioning paths; a 404 on the exchange fails the\nbeat and names the route (host < module-saas-starter v0.0.61 is not\nsupported, or the URL is wrong). Removes the probe spacing, the exchanged\nlatch and the ambiguous-boot check that only existed to serve the fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: close the credential-exfiltration and misattribution holes in solution registration\n\nReview of the publisher-bound registration work found ten defects. Each fix\nbelow addresses the cause, not the symptom, and each behaviour change is pinned\nby a test verified to fail against the previous code.\n\nSecurity — the registration secrets could be walked off to another host.\nregistrationClient set no CheckRedirect, so a registration request followed\nredirects. net/http strips only Authorization, WWW-Authenticate and Cookie\nacross hosts; every custom header is copied verbatim, and 307/308 re-sends the\nbody with them. Anything able to answer at a registration URL with a Location\nwas handed the plaintext solution secret and the cluster-internal token — the\nexact credential this publisher binding exists to protect — and the theft\nlooked like an ordinary beat. Redirects are now refused, as proxying already\nwas, for the same reason.\n\nCorrectness — a registration could outlive the token it presented.\nsolutionTokenMinimumLifetime (1s) was justified as \"enough to outlive the\nPOST\", but the POST is bounded by registrationTimeout (10s). A 2s token — a\nlifetime the tests bless — presented to a host answering in 3s arrived expired\nand came back 401, which invalidate() then reported as an id owned by another\npublisher, sending the reader to check publisher ownership for a clock problem.\nauthorize now returns the credential''s expiry and beat bounds the request by\nit, so the case surfaces as that credential''s own named deadline. The same\nlatent bug in moduleCredential (a cached token is presented with as little as\nhalf its lifetime left) is fixed by the same mechanism.\n\nDiagnostics — three boot failures named the wrong cause.\n* Serve swallowed codefly.LoadEnvironmentVariables()''s error. Every SDK-resolved\n  value is empty when that load fails, so validate() told the operator to\n  provision a secret that was already provisioned. The error is now carried into\n  config and reported instead. (The comment claiming this was\n  \"secretProvisioningUnknown''s job\" named a function that has never existed.)\n* GATEWAY_REGISTER_URL was free-form until the exchange began deriving from it;\n  an override not ending in /solutions/_register now fails the boot, and did so\n  reporting an unresolved SDK endpoint. It now names the variable that changed.\n* A secret carrying the trailing newline a file-mounted value almost always has\n  passed validate() and then made net/http refuse to write the header, so the\n  beat failed forever with correct provisioning. Secrets are trimmed.\n\nAvailability — a gateway outage removed the solution from a healthy host.\nBoth self-registrations now mint through the gateway, so a gateway restart also\nfails the host-frontend registration. On the 2m cap that left the solution out\nof a healthy host''s nav for up to 2m24s after the gateway returned. That cap\nexists to bound audited mints, and a beat that never reached its surface minted\nnothing — those now retry on a 30s cap. backoff also stops shortening an\ninterval already slower than the cap, which the new cap made reachable.\n\nLog throttling — the dedup key was text the host chooses. A refusal quoting\nsomething per-attempt (the jti of the single-use token it just burned) differs\nevery beat by construction, defeating the throttle exactly when registration is\nmost broken. Distinct reasons per status are now bounded, and the suppression\nis announced rather than silent.\n\nAlso: /.well-known/capabilities hardcoded the contract majors the registration\nmanifest takes from constants, so bumping a constant would have left one\nsolution claiming two different contracts; internalTokenAuth, the fallback this\nruntime removed, was dead production code still documented as the\nself-registration credential, and is now a test stub so it cannot be rewired in\none line; selfRegistrationCredentials gave a wrong reason (jti races) for a\nright decision (an unlocked struct is not shareable); and a beat is no longer\nfree, so CODEFLY__SOLUTION_REGISTRATION_INTERVAL exposes the beat period — the\ndefault is unchanged, because the right value depends on the host''s\nregistration TTL, which this runtime cannot observe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"ecf32b84902d61743fbbf7846ae87f25a28e3c25","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/ecf32b84902d61743fbbf7846ae87f25a28e3c25"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6","verification":{"payload":"tree ecf32b84902d61743fbbf7846ae87f25a28e3c25\nparent 0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1789128356 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789128356 -0400\n\nfeat!: fail closed on solution registration — no cluster-internal-token fallback (#26)\n\n* feat!: fail closed on solution registration — no cluster-internal-token fallback\n\nThe shared cluster-internal token proves no publisher, so it is never\npresented on a registration. A boot without a provisioned secret is refused\nby validate(), naming the provisioning paths; a 404 on the exchange fails the\nbeat and names the route (host < module-saas-starter v0.0.61 is not\nsupported, or the URL is wrong). Removes the probe spacing, the exchanged\nlatch and the ambiguous-boot check that only existed to serve the fallback.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: close the credential-exfiltration and misattribution holes in solution registration\n\nReview of the publisher-bound registration work found ten defects. Each fix\nbelow addresses the cause, not the symptom, and each behaviour change is pinned\nby a test verified to fail against the previous code.\n\nSecurity — the registration secrets could be walked off to another host.\nregistrationClient set no CheckRedirect, so a registration request followed\nredirects. net/http strips only Authorization, WWW-Authenticate and Cookie\nacross hosts; every custom header is copied verbatim, and 307/308 re-sends the\nbody with them. Anything able to answer at a registration URL with a Location\nwas handed the plaintext solution secret and the cluster-internal token — the\nexact credential this publisher binding exists to protect — and the theft\nlooked like an ordinary beat. Redirects are now refused, as proxying already\nwas, for the same reason.\n\nCorrectness — a registration could outlive the token it presented.\nsolutionTokenMinimumLifetime (1s) was justified as \"enough to outlive the\nPOST\", but the POST is bounded by registrationTimeout (10s). A 2s token — a\nlifetime the tests bless — presented to a host answering in 3s arrived expired\nand came back 401, which invalidate() then reported as an id owned by another\npublisher, sending the reader to check publisher ownership for a clock problem.\nauthorize now returns the credential''s expiry and beat bounds the request by\nit, so the case surfaces as that credential''s own named deadline. The same\nlatent bug in moduleCredential (a cached token is presented with as little as\nhalf its lifetime left) is fixed by the same mechanism.\n\nDiagnostics — three boot failures named the wrong cause.\n* Serve swallowed codefly.LoadEnvironmentVariables()''s error. Every SDK-resolved\n  value is empty when that load fails, so validate() told the operator to\n  provision a secret that was already provisioned. The error is now carried into\n  config and reported instead. (The comment claiming this was\n  \"secretProvisioningUnknown''s job\" named a function that has never existed.)\n* GATEWAY_REGISTER_URL was free-form until the exchange began deriving from it;\n  an override not ending in /solutions/_register now fails the boot, and did so\n  reporting an unresolved SDK endpoint. It now names the variable that changed.\n* A secret carrying the trailing newline a file-mounted value almost always has\n  passed validate() and then made net/http refuse to write the header, so the\n  beat failed forever with correct provisioning. Secrets are trimmed.\n\nAvailability — a gateway outage removed the solution from a healthy host.\nBoth self-registrations now mint through the gateway, so a gateway restart also\nfails the host-frontend registration. On the 2m cap that left the solution out\nof a healthy host''s nav for up to 2m24s after the gateway returned. That cap\nexists to bound audited mints, and a beat that never reached its surface minted\nnothing — those now retry on a 30s cap. backoff also stops shortening an\ninterval already slower than the cap, which the new cap made reachable.\n\nLog throttling — the dedup key was text the host chooses. A refusal quoting\nsomething per-attempt (the jti of the single-use token it just burned) differs\nevery beat by construction, defeating the throttle exactly when registration is\nmost broken. Distinct reasons per status are now bounded, and the suppression\nis announced rather than silent.\n\nAlso: /.well-known/capabilities hardcoded the contract majors the registration\nmanifest takes from constants, so bumping a constant would have left one\nsolution claiming two different contracts; internalTokenAuth, the fallback this\nruntime removed, was dead production code still documented as the\nself-registration credential, and is now a test stub so it cannot be rewired in\none line; selfRegistrationCredentials gave a wrong reason (jti races) for a\nright decision (an unlocked struct is not shareable); and a beat is no longer\nfree, so CODEFLY__SOLUTION_REGISTRATION_INTERVAL exposes the beat period — the\ndefault is unchanged, because the right value depends on the host''s\nregistration TTL, which this runtime cannot observe.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo+6kCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAuzMQACOy9RDpMpPvtApdeZHsQf4S\nFP53/0VWiJ4XPPpMDa0dJXNGaUTLNe0phOsOYdE97PokARbBgpq/jhh0q5qc2Ccl\ndxEqKu8F5yMbaOGi3oU9jSghO1VvEOFb57etzbegsEjefEC2PSQ7IGYxm+EApKeB\nDqKdszLUVIyM+FtEw7uQ8BrgRMmmYSvRWkiPjBBxQGzJW2zAsS6yEpweX+IiNogk\nPtZKLWdjqopxE+rccjWDG08BVSKJSOeGJOM66fCUQ7GJZoswcsAFh+uHNX+dNBl8\nHjXyeolbFlgOH0chV+vZf8E7S/auJMr4WPtZhGF37kdBibeiSWPODin6h97vdZ4D\nUpJL8NM6avSFgyDuq5ofJgi4qNrhDxLJAg2kaBxqhZnou9jjSznANidDPxnyn/UJ\nkF5MB61PNv7dSskuZb56rsVpyxOyJe9zfRlFSPJu/vxcXTRXTKWsWgRrc4e0F6t9\ntkSqfj6f2N4G5tKiQlznHT1nDKvYroZKwDeezRz8YQF9f1dyjCYvwgO3SQB/IgAw\nGxG36cYy8Oa8lwbqftXvep7q/o9bCoINQAcDtsYVWmHbcGV5CEunopbfrlrgntQH\nwo+dK5GtaHa8rsBXhEsKW8TTOGNcM1VCtwiIde8tSTbLUxmSWal0rCL5qfUL9AZW\ncsfSFqsptXYX68fjfgy0\n=asbE\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T12:05:57Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKGUxZGE1MTIwZThjNTFhOGM4NzU4MTM2MDM4ODM5NzhmMjVjYzZhZTY","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025","sha":"0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025"}],"sha":"e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/e1da5120e8c51a8c875813603883978f25cc6ae6"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-11T03:26:08Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-11T03:26:08Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: mint and present the solution''s publisher-bound registration credential (#24) (#25)\n\n* feat: mint and present the solution''s publisher-bound registration credential (#24)\n\nmodule-saas-starter v0.0.61 (#540) binds solution registration to the\npublisher: /solutions/_register and /api/solutions/register admit a\nregistration only against a signed, solution-bound token minted by\n/solutions/_registration-token to a caller presenting the registration\nsecret the composition declared for that id, and refuse the shared\ncluster-internal token. The runtime still presented the latter, so against\nsuch a host every beat was refused and no solution was served.\n\n- solutionCredential: exchanges the solution secret (plus the internal\n  token, the gateway''s perimeter check) for the token and presents it as\n  X-Codefly-Solution-Registration. Both surfaces burn a token on use, so a\n  fresh one is minted per beat per surface; a refusal of a fresh token is\n  diagnosed once as not-staleness.\n- The secret resolves through the SDK as the `solution-registration`\n  workspace secret''s `SECRET` (CODEFLY__SOLUTION_REGISTRATION_SECRET as an\n  explicit override); the exchange URL follows the gateway register URL and\n  is validated at boot only when a secret makes the exchange part of it.\n- Without a secret the runtime registers as before (internal token) and\n  logs which half of the provisioning is missing.\n- A refusal carrying reasons (409 incompatible_runtime) is logged with them.\n- The manifest declares schemaVersion 1 and frontend.hostContract 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: fall back to the cluster-internal token against a host with no exchange\n\nA host from before the publisher-bound contract answers 404 on\n/solutions/_registration-token and still admits the internal token, so a\ncomposition that already provisioned its secret keeps booting against it;\nthe exchange is retried on every beat so a host upgrade is picked up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: settle the fallback''s cause from the registration''s outcome, not the 404\n\nReview of the publisher-bound credential found the compatibility fallback\nasserting two things a 404 cannot establish, plus a lifetime floor that\nrejected the credentials this design expects. Fixed in severity order.\n\nThe fallback misdiagnosed a current host reached at a wrong exchange URL. A\n404 was read as \"this host predates v0.0.61\", and invalidate() then reported\n\"the exchange accepted this solution''s secret\" for a beat where nothing was\nminted — three log lines, two false, all pointing away from the URL, while the\nsolution was never served. A 404 alone cannot tell an old host from a bad URL;\nthe registration that follows can, because the first accepts the internal\ntoken and the second refuses it. So the notice now names both readings and\ninvalidate() reports the disproof: the refusal proves the host is not an old\none, so the route is the fault and neither provisioning nor publisher\nownership is implicated.\n\nsolutionTokenMinimumLifetime was 5s, copied from moduleTokenMinimumLifetime —\nwhere the token is cached across beats. This one is presented on the very next\nround trip, so the floor bounds one request: at 5s an issuer minting genuinely\nsingle-use seconds-scale tokens failed every beat forever, blaming this host''s\nclock. Now 1s.\n\nThe refusal reason was plumbed through beat and then deduped on the status\nalone, so a host answering 409 while changing why said it once and went silent\non every later reason. The reason is now part of the dedup key.\n\nThe 404 probe never decayed. A host that truly has no route 404s for as long\nas it runs and accepts the beat that follows, so the heartbeat''s backoff never\nwidens — the credential re-asked a known-absent route every beat, on both\nheartbeats, for the life of the process. It now spaces out to 2 minutes, still\npicking an upgrade up without a restart.\n\nAn empty secret meant both \"none provisioned\" and \"the SDK never loaded the\nenvironment it would have come from\"; WorkspaceSecret returns the same error\neither way, so the error cannot separate them and the load failure is the only\nsignal that can. Booting on the wrong reading came up healthy — port bound,\n/health 200 — registered with a credential the host refuses, and blamed\nprovisioning that may be correct. Now refused at boot, and only in that\nambiguous case: a resolved secret or a clean load is untouched.\n\nAlso: once a host has answered the exchange, a later 404 fails the beat rather\nthan downgrading, so an unauthenticated 404 can no longer trade the\npublisher-bound credential for the shared cluster-internal token; the mint\ncount is reported periodically, since the no-cache design rests on the host\nburning a token per surface and its cost was observable only on the issuer;\nheartbeat waits are jittered, because both credentials otherwise minted in\nlockstep every beat; a host''s refusal reasons are flattened so one cannot forge\na log line; and moduleTokenExchangeTimeout is renamed\nregistrationExchangeTimeout, which is what it bounds for both credentials.\n\nThe fake host''s `legacy` flag welded \"no exchange route\" to \"admits the\ninternal token\", making the host that matters most — one that 404s the exchange\nand refuses the internal token — unreachable by construction. Split into two\nknobs, and every fix above is covered by a test that fails without it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"4b01b0fbae03ee511062fa6601b59b5855a76042","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/4b01b0fbae03ee511062fa6601b59b5855a76042"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025","verification":{"payload":"tree 4b01b0fbae03ee511062fa6601b59b5855a76042\nparent 36aca19b62c414c63fc1c3f497e04c5043004d5c\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1789097168 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789097168 -0400\n\nfeat: mint and present the solution''s publisher-bound registration credential (#24) (#25)\n\n* feat: mint and present the solution''s publisher-bound registration credential (#24)\n\nmodule-saas-starter v0.0.61 (#540) binds solution registration to the\npublisher: /solutions/_register and /api/solutions/register admit a\nregistration only against a signed, solution-bound token minted by\n/solutions/_registration-token to a caller presenting the registration\nsecret the composition declared for that id, and refuse the shared\ncluster-internal token. The runtime still presented the latter, so against\nsuch a host every beat was refused and no solution was served.\n\n- solutionCredential: exchanges the solution secret (plus the internal\n  token, the gateway''s perimeter check) for the token and presents it as\n  X-Codefly-Solution-Registration. Both surfaces burn a token on use, so a\n  fresh one is minted per beat per surface; a refusal of a fresh token is\n  diagnosed once as not-staleness.\n- The secret resolves through the SDK as the `solution-registration`\n  workspace secret''s `SECRET` (CODEFLY__SOLUTION_REGISTRATION_SECRET as an\n  explicit override); the exchange URL follows the gateway register URL and\n  is validated at boot only when a secret makes the exchange part of it.\n- Without a secret the runtime registers as before (internal token) and\n  logs which half of the provisioning is missing.\n- A refusal carrying reasons (409 incompatible_runtime) is logged with them.\n- The manifest declares schemaVersion 1 and frontend.hostContract 1.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* feat: fall back to the cluster-internal token against a host with no exchange\n\nA host from before the publisher-bound contract answers 404 on\n/solutions/_registration-token and still admits the internal token, so a\ncomposition that already provisioned its secret keeps booting against it;\nthe exchange is retried on every beat so a host upgrade is picked up.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: settle the fallback''s cause from the registration''s outcome, not the 404\n\nReview of the publisher-bound credential found the compatibility fallback\nasserting two things a 404 cannot establish, plus a lifetime floor that\nrejected the credentials this design expects. Fixed in severity order.\n\nThe fallback misdiagnosed a current host reached at a wrong exchange URL. A\n404 was read as \"this host predates v0.0.61\", and invalidate() then reported\n\"the exchange accepted this solution''s secret\" for a beat where nothing was\nminted — three log lines, two false, all pointing away from the URL, while the\nsolution was never served. A 404 alone cannot tell an old host from a bad URL;\nthe registration that follows can, because the first accepts the internal\ntoken and the second refuses it. So the notice now names both readings and\ninvalidate() reports the disproof: the refusal proves the host is not an old\none, so the route is the fault and neither provisioning nor publisher\nownership is implicated.\n\nsolutionTokenMinimumLifetime was 5s, copied from moduleTokenMinimumLifetime —\nwhere the token is cached across beats. This one is presented on the very next\nround trip, so the floor bounds one request: at 5s an issuer minting genuinely\nsingle-use seconds-scale tokens failed every beat forever, blaming this host''s\nclock. Now 1s.\n\nThe refusal reason was plumbed through beat and then deduped on the status\nalone, so a host answering 409 while changing why said it once and went silent\non every later reason. The reason is now part of the dedup key.\n\nThe 404 probe never decayed. A host that truly has no route 404s for as long\nas it runs and accepts the beat that follows, so the heartbeat''s backoff never\nwidens — the credential re-asked a known-absent route every beat, on both\nheartbeats, for the life of the process. It now spaces out to 2 minutes, still\npicking an upgrade up without a restart.\n\nAn empty secret meant both \"none provisioned\" and \"the SDK never loaded the\nenvironment it would have come from\"; WorkspaceSecret returns the same error\neither way, so the error cannot separate them and the load failure is the only\nsignal that can. Booting on the wrong reading came up healthy — port bound,\n/health 200 — registered with a credential the host refuses, and blamed\nprovisioning that may be correct. Now refused at boot, and only in that\nambiguous case: a resolved secret or a clean load is untouched.\n\nAlso: once a host has answered the exchange, a later 404 fails the beat rather\nthan downgrading, so an unauthenticated 404 can no longer trade the\npublisher-bound credential for the shared cluster-internal token; the mint\ncount is reported periodically, since the no-cache design rests on the host\nburning a token per surface and its cost was observable only on the issuer;\nheartbeat waits are jittered, because both credentials otherwise minted in\nlockstep every beat; a host''s refusal reasons are flattened so one cannot forge\na log line; and moduleTokenExchangeTimeout is renamed\nregistrationExchangeTimeout, which is what it bounds for both credentials.\n\nThe fake host''s `legacy` flag welded \"no exchange route\" to \"admits the\ninternal token\", making the host that matters most — one that 404s the exchange\nand refuses the internal token — unreachable by construction. Split into two\nknobs, and every fix above is covered by a test that fails without it.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqo3TQCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAOfEQAEjefKWwTIFlCIm1ViUaIDY1\nfzDelgunan40FjRGiiLYYgbX4gcZR3iImUbWj61XvlrVBMuLm4edt9kovqyZ3OfS\n1aOZcbHWDNXfgT5ZGlcg+8Th3nNDTQpwoCXpEpUGAJtWZiRlbgdwNIY6l/U5cKZE\n/i4oCx5goAbyBlDGftkI8J4JU2Ev5BPLzUScD5F1C55eV7U9c4rj3Cf98OmsYY20\nDA0W720eIaqpEPDvG+dKRgJT35ReXzdDDWsiqimcepVpKERnmo+emsPuSAnrmfnU\nYexwa1fop4BpLXGgtI08RoDAPNLI8h+6VFEJH/176k49peEDbLjtTvY69GNDU517\np5FDsL+Yzzz2dW+xDe1iUIAS+m6Y8bfmdnr7hpo+HXjgp61YeD9bD8KU8pB4QWCB\nH+k9V0Nv86Imh3uzx2cEFyGWd+3HTHL1UwasVRCmO7CkotgDaTdpBwxHpbNODgR8\n+gWq/ni27LwlAkO1f+HLNZPL/A+BP1XqjbJjGDRyFk1PVpv6JOphVJse56a2QFVk\ndU5lBoECGlflvVcWpuKtgnH/2d8BVnxFzS6NYuUkd7BoInaJ5hnUUmbPXlLnduTt\nK9XAl6kPB1+rvPjzrroR+xluSuw9yBfWZVUNnPDEPkBoEV63Cj+05d5KK3JcErwf\nQhGhEHBafIezfaKpsk3+\n=zHkt\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-11T03:26:09Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDBkMDg1MWMwNmQ4NjU0OWY4YWViMzMzYTRiYWVhZGVjZmY2NzkwMjU","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/36aca19b62c414c63fc1c3f497e04c5043004d5c","sha":"36aca19b62c414c63fc1c3f497e04c5043004d5c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/36aca19b62c414c63fc1c3f497e04c5043004d5c"}],"sha":"0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/0d0851c06d86549f8aeb333a4baeadecff679025"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/36aca19b62c414c63fc1c3f497e04c5043004d5c/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:49:54Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-10T14:49:54Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: mint and present the viewer''s Work Context for module reads (#22) (#23)\n\n* feat: mint and present the viewer''s Work Context for module reads (#22)\n\nGateway forwarded only the viewer''s bearer, so a module that authenticates\nby signed Work Context — deriving tenant and subject from\nx-codefly-work-context — refused every solution → module read. The gateway\nverifies and forwards a presented context but mints none, so the runtime\nmints it.\n\nForModule derives a gateway for one module: a Task Work Context minted\nthrough accounts'' StartTask with the forwarded bearer (viewer as both owner\nand actor, the module as audience, the requested scopes as the authority),\npresented alongside the bearer on every request. Capabilities are cached per\n(org, audience, scopes) for the life of the request and honour the issuer''s\nexpiry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve the viewer''s Work Context per request and refuse an unusable expiry (#22)\n\nReview of the ForModule implementation found the caching layer wrong in three\nways that all present as success.\n\nThe cache compared the issuer''s expiry against this host''s clock with a fixed\n10s renewal lead, so a skewed clock, an issuer TTL under 10s, or an absent\nexpiresAt each made every lookup miss — correct answers, no error, no log, and\none audited mint per read. exchange() 200 lines above already refuses an\nunusable expiry, names the protobuf-JSON spelling, reports clock skew\nseparately, and clamps the lead to half the credential''s life; mint now does\nthe same.\n\nThe derived gateway snapshotted its capability, so a handler holding one past\nthe TTL sent a stale context that the edge rejects before routing — worse than\nthe bearer-only client it replaced, since that at least reached the module. It\nnow holds the ask and resolves a capability per round trip.\n\nConcurrent asks for one capability each ran their own mint, against a doc\npromising \"one ask mints once\". The cache now dedups mints in flight per ask,\nand a waiter takes the leader''s outcome rather than retrying its failure.\n\nAlso: the mint runs on a bearer-only client, so a capability minted for one\nmodule no longer rides along on the request minting another''s (harmless until\nthe first lapses, then it 401s the call meant to replace it); gateway traffic\nuses the non-proxying transport registration traffic already uses, so the\nviewer''s bearer cannot be dialled to an arbitrary egress host; the no-org\nrefusal names the present-but-empty case the gateway actually produces; and\nScope drops its JSON tags for an internal wire type, keeping accounts'' field\nspellings out of this package''s public API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"0b65b61bab966c194ce7df141b875a668ba47a44","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/0b65b61bab966c194ce7df141b875a668ba47a44"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/36aca19b62c414c63fc1c3f497e04c5043004d5c","verification":{"payload":"tree 0b65b61bab966c194ce7df141b875a668ba47a44\nparent c0b787251cf78190fad4cce012bff07671fc7c9c\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1789051794 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1789051794 -0400\n\nfeat: mint and present the viewer''s Work Context for module reads (#22) (#23)\n\n* feat: mint and present the viewer''s Work Context for module reads (#22)\n\nGateway forwarded only the viewer''s bearer, so a module that authenticates\nby signed Work Context — deriving tenant and subject from\nx-codefly-work-context — refused every solution → module read. The gateway\nverifies and forwards a presented context but mints none, so the runtime\nmints it.\n\nForModule derives a gateway for one module: a Task Work Context minted\nthrough accounts'' StartTask with the forwarded bearer (viewer as both owner\nand actor, the module as audience, the requested scopes as the authority),\npresented alongside the bearer on every request. Capabilities are cached per\n(org, audience, scopes) for the life of the request and honour the issuer''s\nexpiry.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve the viewer''s Work Context per request and refuse an unusable expiry (#22)\n\nReview of the ForModule implementation found the caching layer wrong in three\nways that all present as success.\n\nThe cache compared the issuer''s expiry against this host''s clock with a fixed\n10s renewal lead, so a skewed clock, an issuer TTL under 10s, or an absent\nexpiresAt each made every lookup miss — correct answers, no error, no log, and\none audited mint per read. exchange() 200 lines above already refuses an\nunusable expiry, names the protobuf-JSON spelling, reports clock skew\nseparately, and clamps the lead to half the credential''s life; mint now does\nthe same.\n\nThe derived gateway snapshotted its capability, so a handler holding one past\nthe TTL sent a stale context that the edge rejects before routing — worse than\nthe bearer-only client it replaced, since that at least reached the module. It\nnow holds the ask and resolves a capability per round trip.\n\nConcurrent asks for one capability each ran their own mint, against a doc\npromising \"one ask mints once\". The cache now dedups mints in flight per ask,\nand a waiter takes the leader''s outcome rather than retrying its failure.\n\nAlso: the mint runs on a bearer-only client, so a capability minted for one\nmodule no longer rides along on the request minting another''s (harmless until\nthe first lapses, then it 401s the call meant to replace it); gateway traffic\nuses the non-proxying transport registration traffic already uses, so the\nviewer''s bearer cannot be dialled to an arbitrary egress host; the no-org\nrefusal names the present-but-empty case the gateway actually produces; and\nScope drops its JSON tags for an internal wire type, keeping accounts'' field\nspellings out of this package''s public API.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqosOSCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAsq0QAD4xwPbUzwHEtmmXOtAVl/bK\nelX4LS+pUHj1e/F77RfxORNvrkUP9sIjqhiZ0mhEKVJHtDAc/DlqcZSfNn5/z0kf\nc2PYTy5KZnTUKLyDe21PpnE2w+RQ6MxUv9ILBzLGZhl/mmt91ImA0ZuoTGxVIrCh\nLolDbdt3fMOZK5aFNdHPWmhgsSgVYCVTtlmoOi2BC6LCgzU/xjCMfTaKLoevrTj+\n/dRs3ZiHkCWaDI5abnwVsb/FjRwNK0H5hFzlFw8eYrS+5jfAeIJhRvcg1wpPVXAv\nGl+XX0slhKFhF6LtzsxAtbTk56bYYpTKa5Oac8w60G4Cnb0AjsVxr5KHVtITyhLv\ntcWmk3TL2ljTadx0hPgA0wEsaI/6pvZfykllH5A7ixyghIrV3ImZPFB/2cw1gfyt\nZ71RoiIyMW41sZxtjzT2FQ83mSCwgTsD5/GA4PSt3h4RgH7hdH92qxTFzxXvFG0r\nspbR8uKBgi1FC6u6Uxt+1JJh7wpcO5rxXoVnZhegvZjkVFNJWTpnZ58ZLexXGcqf\nzzwQhRwXlClWHxrSks3oVcssQqMvP9SIaG91XmrgakjYeKN7qHIEswyvIqKxesDD\ndR0HRb/KwQX2tdAlaMydMIpqD3iBHQz4s+tz5ZjcwktTfxNRoJiAC8lrQRR5iOJP\nUaAxYcS28PpqtE26y32A\n=s831\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"verified_at":"2026-09-10T14:49:55Z"}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/19864447?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/u