untime-go/commits/039f035e0aec1edd71dfba86ddcd7fd3f69e6cf2"}],"sha":"c0b787251cf78190fad4cce012bff07671fc7c9c","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/c0b787251cf78190fad4cce012bff07671fc7c9c"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/039f035e0aec1edd71dfba86ddcd7fd3f69e6cf2/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:41:06Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-09T15:41:06Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: present the signed module-registration token to the gateway (#101) (#19)\n\n* feat: present the signed module-registration token to the gateway (#101)\n\nModule registrations posted the shared cluster-internal token, which the\ngateway refuses on /modules/_register: it admits a registration only against a\nshort-lived token accounts signs and binds to a single prefix. Every consumed\nmodule therefore 401''d and its /v1/<prefix>/* stayed unrouted.\n\nThe runtime now runs the exchange the gateway brokers — presenting the\nregistration secret its composition provisioned for that prefix — and registers\nwith the token it gets back. The token is cached until shortly before expiry, so\na 15s beat does not re-mint an audited security event four times a minute, and\ndropped when a registration is refused so a gateway that has stopped honouring\nit is recovered from on the next beat rather than after the full lifetime.\n\nThe credential is per consumed module, so a missing secret or a refused exchange\nfails only that module''s registration: siblings still federate and the backend\nkeeps serving. A prefix with no provisioned secret is skipped with a log naming\nCODEFLY__MODULE_REGISTRATION_SECRETS, because every beat would otherwise be a\nguaranteed 401 and the real gap is provisioning, not the runtime.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: refuse an unusable expiry, unshare the beat interval, stop proxying (#101)\n\nReview of the first cut found four defects, each fixed at its cause.\n\nexchange validated the token but not the expiry, so a response carrying none\nwas cached as \"already expired\" and re-run on the very next beat — while every\nregistration still returned 200. That is a mint, and an audited security event\non the issuer, four times a minute for the life of the process, with nothing in\nthe log after the first success. An absent field decodes to the zero time (an\nunset timestamp upstream, or a rename to the protobuf JSON spelling), and a\nclock skewed past the credential''s own lifetime lands in the same place. An\nexpiry this process cannot act on is now a boundary error, not a cache entry.\n\nregistrationInterval was a package var a test wrote while heartbeat goroutines\nfrom earlier tests still read it — serve does not wait for them, and the loop\nevaluates the interval before the select observes a cancelled context. Racy by\nconstruction, and this repo runs no CI, so a single lucky -race run was the only\nthing standing behind it. The interval is now per-Server, which removes the\nsharing rather than the symptom.\n\nRegistration ran on http.DefaultClient, whose ProxyFromEnvironment would dial an\narbitrary egress host with the module''s plaintext secret, the cluster-internal\ntoken, and the signed token that decides where a prefix''s authenticated traffic\ngoes. The issuing side of this same exchange refuses proxying for exactly this\nreason. All registration traffic now uses a transport with no proxy: every\ntarget is composition-local and none of them may be proxied.\n\nThe two federation endpoints could address different gateways: an explicit\nGATEWAY_MODULE_REGISTER_URL moved registration while the exchange stayed on the\nresolved gateway, minting against one host to register with another that never\ntrusts the result. The token URL now follows the register URL''s origin.\n\nThe secrets parser trimmed the entry but not its halves, so \"documents :\ns3cret\" — a pair the registrar accepts, since it trims both — was keyed under\n\"documents \" here and silently missed every lookup.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: bound the credential exchange, and stop deriving a wrong token URL (#101)\n\nRound-three review of the module-registration credential found that every\nfailure on the exchange path converged on the same behaviour — run the whole\nexchange again on the next beat — so one broken deployment became a mint, and\nan audited security event on accounts, four times a minute per module, forever.\nMeasured against the fake gateway: 214 mints in 300ms of beats on a\npermanently-refused registration, and 141 exchanges answered by a single log\nline when the issuer returned no expiry. The round-two guard did not prevent\nthat second one: the mint happens on the issuer before this process ever sees\nthe expiry, so refusing to cache the result changed only whether the\nregistration succeeded, not how often a token was minted.\n\nThree fixes, at the cause rather than the symptom:\n\n- A refusal now buys exactly one re-mint. Staleness is the single cause a fresh\n  token repairs, and a token minted for the very beat that was refused cannot be\n  stale — so a 401/403 on one is kept and diagnosed rather than answered with\n  another mint. A successful registration closes the episode, so an independent\n  later refusal still earns its own retry.\n- Failing beats back off, doubling to a two-minute cap and resetting on the\n  first success. This bounds every other route into the same loop — a refused\n  exchange, an unusable response — without ever giving up on recovery.\n- No registration request is unbounded. registrationClient carried no Timeout\n  and the beat context has no deadline, so a gateway that accepted a\n  registration and never answered blocked the beat in Do forever: that module,\n  or this whole solution when it happened on a self-registration, silently\n  stopped registering for the life of the process, with no log and no recovery.\n\nSame measurements after: 2 mints and 8 exchanges.\n\nAlso, siblingURL rebuilt the token URL from scheme+host, dropping everything\nbetween the host and the endpoint. A gateway served under a path prefix\n(GATEWAY_URL=http://gateway:8080/gw) registered at /gw/modules/_register while\nexchanging at /modules/_registration-token — still absolute, so validate()\npassed it, and a 404 on every beat after that. It now swaps the known path\nsuffix, keeping the prefix, and refuses to guess when the override is not\npairable so validate() names the URL the operator must set.\n\nAnd three smaller ones the same review named: 403 drops a credential like 401,\nso a lapsed token is not replayed for the rest of its life; the 30s renewal lead\nis a ceiling on how early we renew rather than a floor on what the issuer may\nissue, so a legitimately short-lived token is honoured (renewed at half its\nlife) instead of refused with a message blaming this host''s clock, and the two\ngenuinely unusable shapes are reported apart because they have different fixes;\nand registration bodies are drained before close so the connection is reused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"fc61cdaa92172372a2f1a28dfba9794896209bf6","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/fc61cdaa92172372a2f1a28dfba9794896209bf6"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/039f035e0aec1edd71dfba86ddcd7fd3f69e6cf2","verification":{"payload":"tree fc61cdaa92172372a2f1a28dfba9794896209bf6\nparent d20035bfd01efd2eb13458f0868c02e581c92e21\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1788968466 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788968466 -0400\n\nfeat: present the signed module-registration token to the gateway (#101) (#19)\n\n* feat: present the signed module-registration token to the gateway (#101)\n\nModule registrations posted the shared cluster-internal token, which the\ngateway refuses on /modules/_register: it admits a registration only against a\nshort-lived token accounts signs and binds to a single prefix. Every consumed\nmodule therefore 401''d and its /v1/<prefix>/* stayed unrouted.\n\nThe runtime now runs the exchange the gateway brokers — presenting the\nregistration secret its composition provisioned for that prefix — and registers\nwith the token it gets back. The token is cached until shortly before expiry, so\na 15s beat does not re-mint an audited security event four times a minute, and\ndropped when a registration is refused so a gateway that has stopped honouring\nit is recovered from on the next beat rather than after 