l earns its own retry.\n- Failing beats back off, doubling to a two-minute cap and resetting on the\n  first success. This bounds every other route into the same loop — a refused\n  exchange, an unusable response — without ever giving up on recovery.\n- No registration request is unbounded. registrationClient carried no Timeout\n  and the beat context has no deadline, so a gateway that accepted a\n  registration and never answered blocked the beat in Do forever: that module,\n  or this whole solution when it happened on a self-registration, silently\n  stopped registering for the life of the process, with no log and no recovery.\n\nSame measurements after: 2 mints and 8 exchanges.\n\nAlso, siblingURL rebuilt the token URL from scheme+host, dropping everything\nbetween the host and the endpoint. A gateway served under a path prefix\n(GATEWAY_URL=http://gateway:8080/gw) registered at /gw/modules/_register while\nexchanging at /modules/_registration-token — still absolute, so validate()\npassed it, and a 404 on every beat after that. It now swaps the known path\nsuffix, keeping the prefix, and refuses to guess when the override is not\npairable so validate() names the URL the operator must set.\n\nAnd three smaller ones the same review named: 403 drops a credential like 401,\nso a lapsed token is not replayed for the rest of its life; the 30s renewal lead\nis a ceiling on how early we renew rather than a floor on what the issuer may\nissue, so a legitimately short-lived token is honoured (renewed at half its\nlife) instead of refused with a message blaming this host''s clock, and the two\ngenuinely unusable shapes are reported apart because they have different fixes;\nand registration bodies are drained before close so the connection is reused.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAA