//github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/d20035bfd01efd2eb13458f0868c02e581c92e21","sha":"d20035bfd01efd2eb13458f0868c02e581c92e21","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/d20035bfd01efd2eb13458f0868c02e581c92e21"}],"sha":"039f035e0aec1edd71dfba86ddcd7fd3f69e6cf2","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/039f035e0aec1edd71dfba86ddcd7fd3f69e6cf2"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/d20035bfd01efd2eb13458f0868c02e581c92e21/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:15:11Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-08T21:15:11Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"feat: register api.consumes module upstreams with the gateway at startup (#17) (#18)\n\n* feat: register api.consumes module upstreams with the gateway at startup (#17)\n\nOn startup, for each of the solution''s api.consumes targets, register the\nmodule''s REST prefix and resolved upstream with the gateway''s module-register\nendpoint using the internal token, so the gateway proxies /v1/<prefix>/* to the\nconsumed module. The upstream is resolved through the SDK (the endpoint carrier\nis injected because the backend depends on the consumed service), the prefix\nmapping comes from core''s CODEFLY__API_CONSUMES projection, and the whole thing\nis a no-op for solutions that declare no api.consumes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: register consumed APIs only under core''s projected facade, not a guessed prefix\n\nregisterConsumedAPIs defaulted an empty `as` to the consumed module name.\nCore defines the facade default as the producing endpoint''s proto package\nshort name (last non-version segment), which it derives at generation time\nand does not project — so the module name is a different value in general.\nTwo concrete failures resulted:\n\n- A bound consume with `as` omitted registered /v1/<module> while the\n  generated client calls /v1/<package-short-name>: every proxied call 404s\n  silently, with nothing failing at boot.\n- Two consumes from the same module with `as` omitted both defaulted to the\n  module name, colliding on one prefix; the gateway''s first-claim-wins left\n  one facade permanently unreachable (a 15s 409 retry loop). Core''s own\n  as-uniqueness check is skipped for empty `as` precisely because it expects\n  the per-endpoint default, not the module name.\n\nThe runtime cannot reconstruct core''s proto-package default from the\nprojected identity, so the real fix is to stop guessing: skip an entry with\nno explicit `as` and log it, rather than register a fabricated prefix that\nmismatches the client or steals another facade''s route. This also removes the\nnow-dead c.Module==\"\" guard (core already filters unbound entries from the\nprojection).\n\nAlso correct the malformed-projection log: ParseConsumedAPIs returns no\nentries on a decode error, so there is no \"rest\" to register — the whole\nfederation is dropped — and the line is reworded to say so loudly.\n\nTests: replace the case that enshrined the module-name default with\nTestServeSkipsConsumedAPIWithoutFacade (empty `as` → no registration); assert\nthe module registration carries the internal token; and pin loadConfig''s\nmoduleRegisterURL default derivation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"cf14893ffc586398492c739dbf41f0fe8d6f66dd","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/cf14893ffc586398492c739dbf41f0fe8d6f66dd"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/d20035bfd01efd2eb13458f0868c02e581c92e21","verification":{"payload":"tree cf14893ffc586398492c739dbf41f0fe8d6f66dd\nparent 8c819de3df3e420d5f565f9a2f255a4721fee39b\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1788902111 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788902111 -0400\n\nfeat: register api.consumes module upstreams with the gateway at startup (#17) (#18)\n\n* feat: register api.consumes module upstreams with the gateway at startup (#17)\n\nOn startup, for each of the solution''s api.consumes targets, register the\nmodule''s REST prefix and resolved upstream with the gateway''s module-register\nendpoint using the internal token, so the gateway proxies /v1/<prefix>/* to the\nconsumed module. The upstream is resolved through the SDK (the endpoint carrier\nis injected because the backend depends on the consumed service), the prefix\nmapping comes from core''s CODEFLY__API_CONSUMES projection, and the whole thing\nis a no-op for solutions that declare no api.consumes.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: register consumed APIs only under core''s projected facade, not a guessed prefix\n\nregisterConsumedAPIs defaulted an empty `as` to the consumed module name.\nCore defines the facade default as the producing endpoint''s proto package\nshort name (last non-version segment), which it derives at generation time\nand does not project — so the module name is a different value in general.\nTwo concrete failures resulted:\n\n- A bound consume with `as` omitted registered /v1/<module> while the\n  generated client calls /v1/<package-short-name>: every proxied call 404s\n  silently, with nothing failing at boot.\n- Two consumes from the same module with `as` omitted both defaulted to the\n  module name, colliding on one prefix; the gateway''s first-claim-wins left\n  one facade permanently unreachable (a 15s 409 retry loop). Core''s own\n  as-uniqueness check is skipped for empty `as` precisely because it expects\n  the per-endpoint default, not the module name.\n\nThe runtime cannot reconstruct core''s proto-package default from the\nprojected identity, so the real fix is to stop guessing: skip an entry with\nno explicit `as` and log it, rather than register a fabricated prefix that\nmismatches the client or steals another facade''s route. This also removes the\nnow-dead c.Module==\"\" guard (core already filters unbound entries from the\nprojection).\n\nAlso correct the malformed-projection log: ParseConsumedAPIs returns no\nentries on a decode error, so there is no \"rest\" to register — the whole\nfederation is dropped — and the line is reworded to say so loudly.\n\nTests: replace the case that enshrined the module-name default with\nTestServeSkipsConsumedAPIWithoutFacade (empty `as` → no registration); assert\nthe module registration carries the internal token; and pin loadConfig''s\nmoduleRegisterURL default derivation.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----