":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/web-flow","id":19864447,"login":"web-flow","node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5ODY0NDQ3","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/web-flow","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/8c819de3df3e420d5f565f9a2f255a4721fee39b","node_id":"C_kwDOT_s2s9oAKDhjODE5ZGUzZGYzZTQyMGQ1ZjU2NWY5YTJmMjU1YTQ3MjFmZWUzOWI","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commit/f5231e88cafd7ab16f14642e2c301993a8b4ff22","sha":"f5231e88cafd7ab16f14642e2c301993a8b4ff22","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/f5231e88cafd7ab16f14642e2c301993a8b4ff22"}],"sha":"8c819de3df3e420d5f565f9a2f255a4721fee39b","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/8c819de3df3e420d5f565f9a2f255a4721fee39b"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/commits/f5231e88cafd7ab16f14642e2c301993a8b4ff22/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T18:55:17Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T18:55:17Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"fix: resolve host by service role, not by workspace module name (#14) (#15)\n\n* fix: resolve host by service role, not by workspace module name (#14)\n\nA solution backend resolved its host gateway/frontend by the host\nmodule''s workspace reference name (CODEFLY_HOST_MODULE, default \"saas\",\nplus a hardcoded [\"saas\",\"saas-starter\"] retry list). That name is a\nworkspace-local alias — the same base-synced host is composed as `saas`\nin one solution and `saas-starter` in another (codefly-dev/core#382) —\nso any name default is wrong for half the solutions, and every host\nrename forced a change here (#10, #12).\n\nResolve by role instead: Codefly injects each endpoint as\nCODEFLY__ENDPOINT__<MODULE>__<SERVICE>__<ENDPOINT>__<API>, and a backend\ndepends on exactly one gateway / one frontend, so hostAddress() scans the\nenv for the role suffix across any single module segment. The host''s\nworkspace name becomes irrelevant; an explicit CODEFLY_HOST_MODULE still\nscopes the lookup when a composition is genuinely ambiguous.\n\nDrops hostModules() and the \"saas\" default. TestLoadConfigResolvesHostByRole\nnow covers saas, saas-starter, and an arbitrary host-module name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve host by role in local runs too, and fail loud on ambiguity\n\nHost-by-role resolution (module unset) only scanned the injected endpoint\nenv carriers. Deployed that works, but in a local run Codefly injects no\ncarriers — endpoints come from the native workspace map — so the scan found\nnothing and the host never resolved, a regression the empty CODEFLY_HOST_MODULE\ndefault introduced against the documented local-native fallback.\n\nReal cause: value resolution short-circuited on the env scan instead of going\nthrough the SDK, so the whole native path was unreachable when the module was\nunset. Split the work in two: discoverHostModule finds the single owning module\n(env carriers when deployed; resources.FindWorkspaceUp + the workspace on disk\nwhen local), then hostAddress delegates the concrete address to the SDK for both\nmodes. This also removes the hardcoded \"CODEFLY__ENDPOINT__\" literal in favor of\nresources.EndpointPrefix.\n\nThe old scan silently returned the first matching env entry when several modules\nexposed the same role — an arbitrary, env-order-dependent host. discoverHostModule\nnow collects distinct owners and returns \"\" on more than one (and on the native\nside treats NonUniqueServiceNameError the same), so validate() fails loud at boot\ninstead of booting against a coin-flip host.\n\nTests: local-native discovery via an on-disk workspace fixture (by-role resolution\nmatches explicit-module resolution), and the ambiguity case (two modules, same\nrole -> empty). README corrected: CODEFLY_HOST_MODULE is empty by default and only\ndisambiguates; the stale .Module(...).Service(...) table rows now describe by-role\nresolution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"f6f67aa6e46b8b0d5fa81f2a5f5a41e3c3fd6166","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/trees/f6f67aa6e46b8b0d5fa81f2a5f5a41e3c3fd6166"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-go/git/commits/f5231e88cafd7ab16f14642e2c301993a8b4ff22","verification":{"payload":"tree f6f67aa6e46b8b0d5fa81f2a5f5a41e3c3fd6166\nparent 22f330bedbe05f736db9b5412f09fa5bd5d60881\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1788807317 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788807317 -0400\n\nfix: resolve host by service role, not by workspace module name (#14) (#15)\n\n* fix: resolve host by service role, not by workspace module name (#14)\n\nA solution backend resolved its host gateway/frontend by the host\nmodule''s workspace reference name (CODEFLY_HOST_MODULE, default \"saas\",\nplus a hardcoded [\"saas\",\"saas-starter\"] retry list). That name is a\nworkspace-local alias — the same base-synced host is composed as `saas`\nin one solution and `saas-starter` in another (codefly-dev/core#382) —\nso any name default is wrong for half the solutions, and every host\nrename forced a change here (#10, #12).\n\nResolve by role instead: Codefly injects each endpoint as\nCODEFLY__ENDPOINT__<MODULE>__<SERVICE>__<ENDPOINT>__<API>, and a backend\ndepends on exactly one gateway / one frontend, so hostAddress() scans the\nenv for the role suffix across any single module segment. The host''s\nworkspace name becomes irrelevant; an explicit CODEFLY_HOST_MODULE still\nscopes the lookup when a composition is genuinely ambiguous.\n\nDrops hostModules() and the \"saas\" default. TestLoadConfigResolvesHostByRole\nnow covers saas, saas-starter, and an arbitrary host-module name.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix: resolve host by role in local runs too, and fail loud on ambiguity\n\nHost-by-role resolution (module unset) only scanned the injected endpoint\nenv carriers. Deployed that works, but in a local run Codefly injects no\ncarriers — endpoints come from the native workspace map — so the scan found\nnothing and the host never resolved, a regression the empty CODEFLY_HOST_MODULE\ndefault introduced against the documented local-native fallback.\n\nReal cause: value resolution short-circuited on the env scan instead of going\nthrough the SDK, so the whole native path was unreachable when the module was\nunset. Split the work in two: discoverHostModule finds the single owning module\n(env carriers when deployed; resources.FindWorkspaceUp + the workspace on disk\nwhen local), then hostAddress delegates the concrete address to the SDK for both\nmodes. This also removes the hardcoded \"CODEFLY__ENDPOINT__\" literal in favor of\nresources.EndpointPrefix.\n\nThe old scan silently returned the first matching env entry when several modules\nexposed the same role — an arbitrary, env-order-dependent host. discoverHostModule\nnow collects distinct owners and returns \"\" on more than one (and on the native\nside treats NonUniqueServiceNameError the same), so validate() fails loud at boot\ninstead of booting against a coin-flip host.\n\nTests: local-native discovery via an on-disk workspace fixture (by-role resolution\nmatches explicit-module resolution), and the ambiguity case (two modules, same\nrole -> empty). README corrected: CODEFLY_HOST_MODULE is empty by default and only\ndisambiguates; the stale .Module(...).Service(...) table rows now describe by-role\nresolution.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnwiVCRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAAJMAQAEwlhwSoIJURoN/l/+slj4T9\nH3zeqNmCvIXSGiy39lUqd97B8fs9BWbY2dLfIlwD8o1Mq3dp0ERRDEd5qHqPadWQ\nclBQ/4dCsuqZFy2+x7OSkNatxXnqj28flNd3ch53sAO5uFG097M2JTB8nzUxPqUo\n774TgSF8E8AUuNx2h+hz57M4MdDqa1yrI/WNspy7xOng7spVdBOAdRsOIK