ithub.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-python/commits/685d27603afd9f250ad16ffcef70435fefaa17bb"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/312536060?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/antoinetoussaint-byte","id":312536060,"login":"antoinetoussaint-byte","node_id":"U_kgDOEqDr_A","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/antoinetoussaint-byte","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-python/commits/4d94d6319dc1b756d838fa2bdcf57f5ee3cdf732/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-09-07T18:45:16Z","email":"antoine.toussaint@obin.ai","name":"antoinetoussaint-byte"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-09-07T18:45:16Z","email":"noreply@github.com","name":"GitHub"},"message":"chore(sdk): shim `solution-sdk sync` over `codefly sync solution-sdk` (#10) (#11)\n\n* chore(sdk): shim solution-sdk sync over codefly sync solution-sdk (#10)\n\n`solution-sdk sync` now hands off to `codefly sync solution-sdk --language\npython` whenever a `solution.codefly.yaml` is present in the manifest''s\ndirectory or any parent up to the workspace root; contracts then resolve from\nthe composed module package instead of a hand-pinned git ref. Without that\nmanifest the legacy fetch-and-vendor path still runs, once, under a deprecation\nwarning. The facade generator stays here until codefly''s proto companion ships\nit; the runtime seam `Gateway.unary(procedure, request, response_type)` is\nunchanged and now pinned by a test against a real recording gateway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WXjyK3Mqp71hTtBfMLo74U\n\n* fix(sdk): clean error on missing codefly, correct README on generator move\n\nReview follow-ups on the solution-sdk shim:\n- exec''s FileNotFoundError (codefly absent) now surfaces as a one-line\n  SystemExit naming codefly, not a raw traceback — the post-migration path\n  is the first thing a migrated solution hits.\n- README no longer claims the facade generator already moved to the proto\n  companion; it hasn''t shipped, so the generator still lives here and\n  protoc-gen-solution_facade is still available. Stated as pending.\n- The in-process legacy test pins _find_solution_manifest to None so it can\n  never take the shim branch and exec away the test runner.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sdk): announce when -f is overridden by the solution.codefly.yaml shim\n\nReview finding #4: when a solution.codefly.yaml is present the shim ignores an\nexplicit `-f legacy.yaml` and hands off to codefly, but did so silently, so a\nuser pointing at a legacy manifest got no signal it was dropped. The shim''s\nprecedence is spec-mandated (the shim must win on migrated solutions), so the\nreal cure is de-silencing, not changing precedence: main() now prints a one-line\nnotice naming the ignored -f, and the --file help documents that it is inert\nonce migrated. Defaulting --file to None distinguishes \"user passed -f\" from the\nimplicit default so the notice fires only when there is something to announce.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","tree":{"sha":"dec4e94b7c3f1dd688506805278269c06ab2259d","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-python/git/trees/dec4e94b7c3f1dd688506805278269c06ab2259d"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/codefly-dev/solution-runtime-python/git/commits/4d94d6319dc1b756d838fa2bdcf57f5ee3cdf732","verification":{"payload":"tree dec4e94b7c3f1dd688506805278269c06ab2259d\nparent 042d489bf88557aa990ea28667fefa448441c06a\nauthor antoinetoussaint-byte <antoine.toussaint@obin.ai> 1788806716 -0400\ncommitter GitHub <noreply@github.com> 1788806716 -0400\n\nchore(sdk): shim `solution-sdk sync` over `codefly sync solution-sdk` (#10) (#11)\n\n* chore(sdk): shim solution-sdk sync over codefly sync solution-sdk (#10)\n\n`solution-sdk sync` now hands off to `codefly sync solution-sdk --language\npython` whenever a `solution.codefly.yaml` is present in the manifest''s\ndirectory or any parent up to the workspace root; contracts then resolve from\nthe composed module package instead of a hand-pinned git ref. Without that\nmanifest the legacy fetch-and-vendor path still runs, once, under a deprecation\nwarning. The facade generator stays here until codefly''s proto companion ships\nit; the runtime seam `Gateway.unary(procedure, request, response_type)` is\nunchanged and now pinned by a test against a real recording gateway.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01WXjyK3Mqp71hTtBfMLo74U\n\n* fix(sdk): clean error on missing codefly, correct README on generator move\n\nReview follow-ups on the solution-sdk shim:\n- exec''s FileNotFoundError (codefly absent) now surfaces as a one-line\n  SystemExit naming codefly, not a raw traceback — the post-migration path\n  is the first thing a migrated solution hits.\n- README no longer claims the facade generator already moved to the proto\n  companion; it hasn''t shipped, so the generator still lives here and\n  protoc-gen-solution_facade is still available. Stated as pending.\n- The in-process legacy test pins _find_solution_manifest to None so it can\n  never take the shim branch and exec away the test runner.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n* fix(sdk): announce when -f is overridden by the solution.codefly.yaml shim\n\nReview finding #4: when a solution.codefly.yaml is present the shim ignores an\nexplicit `-f legacy.yaml` and hands off to codefly, but did so silently, so a\nuser pointing at a legacy manifest got no signal it was dropped. The shim''s\nprecedence is spec-mandated (the shim must win on migrated solutions), so the\nreal cure is de-silencing, not changing precedence: main() now prints a one-line\nnotice naming the ignored -f, and the --file help documents that it is inert\nonce migrated. Defaulting --file to None distinguishes \"user passed -f\" from the\nimplicit default so the notice fires only when there is something to announce.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>","reason":"valid","signature":"-----BEGIN PGP SIGNATURE-----\n\nwsFcBAABCAAQBQJqnwY8CRC1aQ7uu5UhlAAA6kcQACjq5Zpl0A8dMRgwnlb1RJJ8\ngC4QqIeDIVR9RYgmQF4reR4GzZLNMtArRSBkeycSxfVyZC3l9qXgOe19llkLUPZC\nCXLwxamvFav+F0RO5u6s7KndS1vr10lqykAevZ/g1w5mOmbDyZM13ztBUPvEfvE+\nYiGMZlh3+oqWEw1H0JVy90xMBRuSJj1Zg3pgIqqLXL1NslAMvn59BwjooBbdmlex\nXpsj4+hxhjcmMeVnk5TqThRZxwDC1dR5OkQG8ac4WRD5nmnpFZ8nUN+jmYS9c/8L\nYdVrANRX1B8/aqkjm08E8EdRgrllSL/aAybYloY/huw7qswOCO0qtIQLkr2v5Vew\nyCry+ljSWPVTHja30opnXspN3UkFUUAhM9pxMb8M7zcAF6LLdHsASvTsVAReZvRw\nvuvQ+gEVmo+hLXsM3qW1UXyC1GCnny1MZv174MMcj1aqskt7BDgikB88wSuUgBT/\nEvUgQrUXvGi20gYDhO/iMiiFh5BX8n+FdyuBvQAUHKa/ZJFXCnm6DN60Y2rttfL1\nWUpCKrZmrn9VDffL9gw64DoMQjrDdtvk8vW04rUCa9GbNIJhubhhhcRKLlPU4r3t\nd+6LEgFXg77GN47iUo0RfQluV6BGmas84FxRBf9c9Lgt0TeN06La6RMcQvGkywnd\nuSn6q+spFnQm968ugojb\n=Yxe2\n-----END PGP SIGNATURE-----\n","verified":true,"ver