ers/akotkaryash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/akotkaryash/developer-companion/commits/528630a0dd44f0c976d36cc5a8e230d4e096f780/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T13:46:15Z","email":"yashakotkar@hotmail.com","name":"akotkaryash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T14:40:31Z","email":"yashakotkar@hotmail.com","name":"akotkaryash"},"message":"feat(contracts): define public REST API contracts (OpenAPI)\n\nDefines the wire contract between the Browser Extension / Angular Web\nShell and the Spring Cloud Gateway: submission ingestion (idempotent on\nuserId+platform+submissionId per the gamification engine''s rules),\nprivate user stats, public profiles, Redis-backed leaderboards, AI\ncoach hints/recommendations, portfolio generation, and admin\nmoderation. Uses RFC 7807 Problem Details for errors (matches Spring\nBoot 3''s built-in ProblemDetail). System health is intentionally left\nout — that''s Actuator''s job, not a bespoke endpoint.\n\nEstablishes contracts/ as the shared source-of-truth directory that\nDEV-202 (internal M2M) and DEV-203 (Kafka/AsyncAPI) will also live in,\nand that DEV-301 will generate typed clients from.\n\nValidated with openapi-spec-validator (OpenAPI 3.0.3, valid).\n\nCloses #21","tree":{"sha":"816ae51994166c0a93cb5885a936a8be4078858e","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/akotkaryash/developer-companion/git/trees/816ae51994166c0a93cb5885a936a8be4078858e"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/akotkaryash/developer-companion/git/commits/528630a0dd44f0c976d36cc5a8e230d4e096f780","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/284685226?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/akotkaryash","id":284685226,"login":"akotkaryash","node_id":"U_kgDOEPfzqg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/akotkaryash/developer-companion/commit/528630a0dd44f0c976d36cc5a8e230d4e096f780","node_id":"C_kwDOT_6kHtoAKDUyODYzMGEwZGQ0NGYwYzk3NmQzNmNjNWE4ZTIzMGQ0ZTA5NmY3ODA","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/akotkaryash/developer-companion/commit/94bab2c1a2ca41023648579a99fc1cf65ae879a1","sha":"94bab2c1a2ca41023648579a99fc1cf65ae879a1","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/akotkaryash/developer-companion/commits/94bab2c1a2ca41023648579a99fc1cf65ae879a1"}],"sha":"528630a0dd44f0c976d36cc5a8e230d4e096f780","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/akotkaryash/developer-companion/commits/528630a0dd44f0c976d36cc5a8e230d4e096f780"},{"author":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/284685226?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/akotkaryash","id":284685226,"login":"akotkaryash","node_id":"U_kgDOEPfzqg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash","user_view_type":"public"},"comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/akotkaryash/developer-companion/commits/94bab2c1a2ca41023648579a99fc1cf65ae879a1/comments","commit":{"author":{"date":"2026-08-27T13:39:41Z","email":"yashakotkar@hotmail.com","name":"akotkaryash"},"comment_count":0,"committer":{"date":"2026-08-27T13:39:41Z","email":"yashakotkar@hotmail.com","name":"akotkaryash"},"message":"docs: expand roadmap to 12 epics with ADR practice and distributed-systems hardening\n\nOriginal roadmap stopped at 6 epics and left several architecturally\nsignificant areas unaccounted for: nothing owned the Gateway/Keycloak\nlayer, nothing built the actual frontend product (libs/feature-*),\nnothing tracked scaling out (Citus sharding, Redis Cluster, multi-instance\ncore service, leader election) despite that being a primary project goal,\nand there was no observability/load-testing pass to actually measure it.\nThere was also no formal integration story for how a new backend service\nor frontend plugin plugs into the platform, and no ADR practice to record\nwhy past decisions (Clean+Microkernel, Kafka as event mesh, Oracle Free\nTier target) were made.\n\nRestructures Phase 4 into 12 epics (Extensibility & Service Integration,\nPlatform Infra & Security, Frontend Plugin Ecosystem, Distributed Systems\nHardening, Observability & Load Testing, and a scoped-down Production\nDeployment added; existing epics renumbered/retained), adds ADRs as a\nstanding practice in Phase 2, and documents the dependency-ordering\nrationale (contracts -> integration strategy -> platform/security ->\nvertical slices -> deliberate hardening -> observability -> deploy).\n\nCompanion GitHub milestones (1-12) and issues (#25-37) were created to\ntrack this structure; DEV-101-204 backfilled onto their milestones.","tree":{"sha":"e43422c3e01903e03f5252f3bea866eaf85c1182","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/akotkaryash/developer-companion/git/trees/e43422c3e01903e03f5252f3bea866eaf85c1182"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/akotkaryash/developer-companion/git/commits/94bab2c1a2ca41023648579a99fc1cf65ae879a1","verification":{"payload":null,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"verified":false,"verified_at":null}},"committer":{"avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/284685226?v=4","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/events{/privacy}","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/gists{/gist_id}","gravatar_id":"","html_url":"https://github.com/akotkaryash","id":284685226,"login":"akotkaryash","node_id":"U_kgDOEPfzqg","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/orgs","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/received_events","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/repos","site_admin":false,"starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash/subscriptions","type":"User","url":"https://api.github.com/users/akotkaryash","user_view_type":"public"},"html_url":"https://github.com/akotkaryash/developer-companion/commit/94bab2c1a2ca41023648579a99fc1cf65ae879a1","node_id":"C_kwDOT_6kHtoAKDk0YmFiMmMxYTJjYTQxMDIzNjQ4NTc5YTk5ZmMxY2Y2NWFlODc5YTE","parents":[{"html_url":"https://github.com/akotkaryash/developer-companion/commit/ef43af0357